erfect Feeding spot.<br /> <br /> See\u2019s what appears to appears to by a 12 to 16 Kindred snaking on some rando drug dealers <br /> MasVamp what are you doing Fledgling I am a 8 generation of the Toreador Clan In my Infinite mercy as you are a Fledgling of a plebeian Clan order you to flee this Territory at once. ReqVamp the fucks a Genration or a Toreador?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T15:31:25-07:00","id":1301168,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, it's always been my headcanon that in the WoD, the End Times came, but instead of destroying the world, it reset the world into what became CofD/nWoD. Hence why the supernaturals that had WoD counterparts seem similar in <i>some</i> ways...but also radically different in other ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T15:31:41-07:00","id":1301169,"title":"","content":"Funded! Let's find out what these stretch goals are!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T16:24:10-07:00","id":1301181,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301169#post1301169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Funded! Let's find out what these stretch goals are!</div> </div> </div> </div>And here we go:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>At $55,000 in funding - CONTAGION CHRONICLE: PLAYER'S COMPANION - &quot;Death&quot;</b> - A <b>Player\u2019s Companion</b> PDF supplement will be created for the <b>Contagion Chronicle</b>, containing a crunchy rules section on supernatural interactions with examples and guidance (ie, &quot;<i>What happens when a Vampire does &quot;X&quot; to a Mage?</i>&quot;). Will be added to the rewards list of all backers receiving the <b>Contagion Chronicle</b> PDF.<br /> <br /> <i>(Don't read too much into the name of this section - &quot;Death&quot; - I was going for a &quot;four horseman&quot; vibe. Let's try to unlock all the horsies over the course of this campaign!)</i> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <b>At $58,000 in funding - CONTAGION CHRONICLE: GLOBAL OUTBREAKS - Alarming Outings</b> - A travelogue supplement PDF will be created for the <b>Contagion Chronicle</b>, adding new locations and new manifestations of the Contagion. Will be added to the rewards list of all backers receiving the <b>Contagion Chronicle</b> PDF.<br /> <br /> <i>And a second supplement as well! </i> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T17:40:23-07:00","id":1301192,"title":"","content":"That players companion sounds like a must have!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24020-mateus","name":"Mateus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24020_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T18:20:31-07:00","id":1301198,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1300870#post1300870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, the Contagion seems to be affecting the thread.<br /> <br /> It still thinks Evil Midnight Lurker is the last poster.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have eerie powers! Involving lurking evilly at midnight. Or maybe lurking at particularly evil midnights?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25206-evil-midnight-lurker","name":"Evil Midnight Lurker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25206_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T18:22:28-07:00","id":1301199,"title":"","content":"Yesssss, yessss, those will be excellent stretch goals. <br /> <br /> Now we just need one for Contagion Dark Eras. Maybe a later goal for Global Outbreaks?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T19:56:09-07:00","id":1301210,"title":"","content":"So the Contagion Chronicle won't deal with crossover mechanics itself; but one of its companion pieces will. <br /> <br /> I can live with that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T20:28:47-07:00","id":1301215,"title":"","content":"I'd figured as much - they've been pretty careful not to claim the book will go over topics like that, which is a kind of conspicuous absence in the messaging.<br /> <br /> It's also not something that I'd really want them to devote core wordcount to anyway, honestly. I'd much rather squeeze in an extra setting. For a companion, though, it's awesome, and I hope the other companions cover similarly-related material that didn't make it into the core.<br /> <br /> Anyone have any wild theories about what we can expect from the other three horsemen of the apocalypse?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 03-30-2019, 11:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T20:42:28-07:00","id":1301219,"title":"","content":"No clue. We're talking about the Player's Companion here, though; so the other Horsemen are other sections of the Companion <i>other than</i> the crossover crunch. <br /> <br /> Or maybe they're different <i>kinds</i> of Crossover Crunch: like where Death his about \u201cwhat happens if an X does Y to Z\u201d, maybe Famine will be about different splats interacting with each others' playgrounds: Mages or Prometheans in the Hedge, vampires or mummies in the Underworld, and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T21:13:32-07:00","id":1301222,"title":"","content":"I believe that was planned for an upcoming book. Dave Brookshaw mentioned one Mage book having details regarding mage and host interaction.<br /> <br /> Might be one about putting normally antagonist folks in groups. Maybe some lost Sworn or False factions, or even Contagions that have 'won' and been excised from reality, leaving the survivors stuck in some hellhole outer world unable to escape.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T21:19:29-07:00","id":1301223,"title":"","content":"I've been wondering what happens if multiple splats try to collaborate on a Safe Space, or whatever the new term is for HQ merits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25206-evil-midnight-lurker","name":"Evil Midnight Lurker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25206_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T21:48:57-07:00","id":1301226,"title":"","content":"You'd just get more dots and bonuses from the Safe Place. 'Unlike most Merits, multiple characters can contribute dots to a single Safe Place, combining their dots into something greater. A Safe Place gives an Initiative bonus equal to the Merit dots. This only applies to a character with dots invested in the Safe Place.'<br /> <br /> From there gamelines have their own Merits that build off of Safe Place but wouldn't really matter for people outside it (like Haven for vampires gives them some bonuses to avoiding Daysleep or waking up when threatened while Daysleeping).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T22:17:03-07:00","id":1301229,"title":"","content":"I'm maybe blind or something, but I do not see 'humans killed by Contagion as ghosts/shades' or Reality Bleed effect in Edinburgh write up... As I'm <b>really</b> not interested in CoD mummies ( my personal thing as ST, simply ), whole Iufenamun simply is to be heck out from my settings. Still, Blightfangs are <i>interesting</i> - and even God-Machine 'antivirus' Grey. But where is this Reality Bleed?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1300815#post1300815\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Iufenamun is <i>not </i>a Contagious, or at least not initially one. He's the main antagonist, yes, but he actually was drawn to the Contagion, which here manifests as Blightfang - a disease that turns people into vampires without the Embrace, and the Grey, the plague the God-Machine made to thin out Blightfang Kindred numbers. He showed up because he thinks he can use the Blightfangs as his army, and he wants to exploit the Reality Bleed effect it has to pull in a world where the Nameless Empire never fell to serve as the capital of a new one. Also, &quot;define what the Contagion symptoms are&quot; seems to be key when designing a setting. We have Blightfangs and Reality Bleed, of course, but it's explicit that's hardly the only one.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1300821#post1300821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yep, any story about Contagion Edinburg is going to involve a story about the demigod that is in the process of learning how to run it. Especially since after another check, he seems to be a native of an alternate universe opened up by the Contagion, one where Amun is a Judge of Duat. Which is way more interesting than just everything being Ten Photographs from Philadelphia all the time (since Iufenamun, while an amoral and diabolic bastard, is an extremely human one as opposed to an alien god; apart from the cultural differences and the Judge he's a normal Su-Menet).</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-30T22:21:36-07:00","id":1301231,"title":"","content":"Tilts (like Reality Bleed) and Conditions (like Blightfang) are at the end of the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T00:54:00-07:00","id":1301242,"title":"","content":"Ship of Theseus and Naglfar\u2019s Army are my two favorite so far, because they are ironically way more similar than any would like to admit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T02:12:51-07:00","id":1301253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301231#post1301231\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tilts (like Reality Bleed) and Conditions (like Blightfang) are at the end of the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>I really want them to release the preview for the Chapter that has these mechanics, because I felt like I was missing context. It's going to drive me up a wall seeing references for Conditions and Tilts or whatever and have no idea what these do until the very end! x.x<br /> <br /> It makes total sense to condense this stuff into the final chapter for the book, but it's gonna be rough getting through the previous chapters for the Kickstarter without it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T03:40:12-07:00","id":1301263,"title":"","content":"Maybe mechanically Reality Bleed is Tilt, but we have firm grasp what if do to the STORY about Blightfangers and Grey from the chapter itself. Here, Reality Bleed seems to be missed in setting itself. Like I literally do not know what Bleed mean here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-31-2019, 09:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T04:56:31-07:00","id":1301270,"title":"","content":"Funded! That first stretch goal is a hell of a choice.<br /> <br /> I'm already excited to salt my popcorn with people complaining about Death being what CC should have been from the start and how y'all are holding it hostage as a Kickstarter stretch goal.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T05:11:29-07:00","id":1301273,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BigDamnHero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301270#post1301270\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm already excited to salt my popcorn with people complaining about Death being what CC should have been from the start and how y'all are holding it hostage as a Kickstarter stretch goal.</div> </div> </div> </div>And they will be COMPLETELY right! I literally started Contagion Chronicle original topic with those words from original answer in Onyx Path Brochure of 2017, when after one year Crossover Chronicle was renamed into Contagion Chronicle. I'm not against the the Contagion idea on itself - I'm rather fond of it - but 'Death' supplement is about what Crossover Chronicle were envisioned in first place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1130339-contagion-chronicle-book#post1130339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From 2017 Onyx Path brochure:<br /> <br /> <i>'The <b>Contagion Chronicle</b> is an overarching Chronicle consisting of chronicle hooks, riveting settings, and Storyteller aids to help present all the <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> game lines into one consistent story. In the chronicle, the Contagion acts as a motivational force and inspires the formation of factions where vampires, werewolves, mages, mummies, etc. come together in new and unique ways.<br /> <br /> Once joined together to deal with the Contagion, these factions will never see their world (or each other) the same way, and will be forever changed. Each time the Contagion emerges to threaten the fabric of our world, the only beings capable of manipulating, slowing, weaponizing, or halting it, are the unnatural denizens from across the <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b>. The Contagion permeates Infrastructure and warps the known antagonists and supporting blocks present in the lives of every inhuman being.'</i><br /> <br /> Year ago it was announced as <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle\">C</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/944730-new-book-the-crossover-chronicle\">rossover Chronicle</a>. I started this new topic as previous have over 25 pages and in this one I wanted to focus on the Contagion ideas and inspirations for the main Chronicle idea in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-31-2019, 09:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T05:54:52-07:00","id":1301285,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konradleijon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301121#post1301121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That\u2019s actually a Cool idea my Headcannon is that the God-Machine was created after the OWOD was destroyed then recreated whitch explains the Edtion differences but also created the Mirror universe /the COfD and it\u2019s the God-Machine\u2019s job to keep them separated. Keep the terminology.<br /> <br /> Edit. Make this a stretch goal!</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> An unrelated idea I had which could be adapted to this is that there are numerous fan splats, so one could do an alternate ChoD with a fansplat filling the niche of an official splat.<br /> <br /> So players might run into an alternate setting where instead of Vampires manipulating things from behind the scenes, Dragons rule their territories, or instead of mages, Geniuses ply their trade, instead of Changelings there are Outsiders altered by the Mythos, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T06:14:26-07:00","id":1301288,"title":"","content":"I do in fact feel a bit cheated, the contagion is fine and all. But I was hoping for mechanical support for running different splats together.<br /> Yeah having a central theme and mood is fine and dandy for a new chronicle. But I already have a game going, theme and mood determined and a unifying aspect that works for me.<br /> Now I'm worried all I'll really get out of this book are the Sworn and the False","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T06:31:24-07:00","id":1301290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Blakemikizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301288#post1301288\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do in fact feel a bit cheated, the contagion is fine and all. But I was hoping for mechanical support for running different splats together.</div> </div> </div> </div>That isn't the fault of the marketing. Pretty much every writer emphasized this is primarily fluff. <br /> <br /> Not all of us can think of good thematic blends either. So not bogging down the core with rules minutia isn't a bad decision.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T06:58:56-07:00","id":1301293,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/contagion-chronicle-a-chronicles-of-darkness-cross/posts/2464893\" target=\"_blank\">Also, the Odense, Denmark preview is up.</a><br /> <br /> Characteristically of the setting of Hamlet, the Contagion here is effectively viral catatonic depression. It's fatal, because its sufferers can't work up the will to finish crossing the street in a busy intersection. Most supernaturals infected are asymptomatic carriers, unless they're vampires, since Patient Zero here is King Knud the Holy, who became a unique Kindred at some point; then the depression not only hits but inflames the Beast (ironically, Beasts themselves are the ones who are most involved in treatment along with Lost, because mortal infected can't feel hope or fear). <br /> <br /> Uniquely, everyone also knows the cure; it's Knud's Touchstone, the pendant he was given at birth. Unfortunately, the King is also the leader of the local Machiavelli Gambit, and they've decided that ruling over mortal shells of people is good governance. Thus, Theseans are playing Van Helsing, desperately trying to find the Pendant and mutate the Contagion into something life-affirming.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T08:30:00-07:00","id":1301317,"title":"","content":"So it's <i>The Happening</i>?<br /> <br /> And on the subject of Death, I don't mind it being \u201cheld hostage\u201d as a stretch goal. A dirty little secret about CoD KS Stretch Goals is that they time them so that all but the last one is a sure thing: the faster the money comes pouring in, the wider the gaps between Stretch Goals, and vice versa. So we're <i>going</i> to get the Player's Companion with at least three of the four Horsemen in it, unless there's a complete and total loss of interest in the KS \u2014 which I have yet to see happen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T10:39:00-07:00","id":1301342,"title":"","content":"I like how the Edinburgh setting was very much Sworn/False versus the contagion itself whereas the Odense setting does a better job of pitting the Sworn and False against each other, shows a good amount of variation between the central antagonists.<br /> <br /> On the subject of the &quot;Death&quot; supplement, pretty much nothing that OPP has said has indicated that the book would deal with the mechanical interactions between splats, since it was branded as the &quot;contagion&quot; they've always indicated it would be pretty much all setting and story stuff. <br /> <br /> Also I'm curious what splat interactions would need much clarification anyway?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25080-kargle18446","name":"Kargle18446","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T10:46:01-07:00","id":1301345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301253#post1301253\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It makes total sense to condense this stuff into the final chapter for the book, but it's gonna be rough getting through the previous chapters for the Kickstarter without it!</div> </div> </div> </div>For the Sin-Eaters kickstarter they released it earlier.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301263#post1301263\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Like I literally do not know what Bleed mean here.</div> </div> </div> </div>Seeping through. If you have a regular piece of paper, and a thick colored marker, when you draw on one side with the marker, sometimes it will bleed through, to the other. This is what's happening.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://farm7.staticflickr.com/6192/6100608693_fd0c9e57d1_b.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T10:52:29-07:00","id":1301347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301290#post1301290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That isn't the fault of the marketing. Pretty much every writer emphasized this is primarily fluff.</div> </div> </div> </div>That won't stop everyone from projecting the Crossover Chronicle they convinced themselves this would be onto Contagion and then being mad that it's not meeting that expectation.<br /> <br /> Things would be so much simpler if people actually paid attention to what things are being advertised as, instead of what it 'would have to include' in their vision.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T10:56:10-07:00","id":1301348,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kargle18446</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301342#post1301342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the subject of the \u201cDeath\u201d supplement, pretty much nothing that OPP has said has indicated that the book would deal with the mechanical interactions between splats, since it was branded as the \u201ccontagion\u201d they've always indicated it would be pretty much all setting and story stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is literally everything we know about the \u201cDeath\u201d supplement so far:<br /> <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">At $55,000 in funding - CONTAGION CHRONICLE: PLAYER'S COMPANION - &quot;Death&quot; - A Player\u2019s Companion PDF supplement will be created for the Contagion Chronicle, containing a crunchy rules section on supernatural interactions with examples and guidance (ie, &quot;What happens when a Vampire does &quot;X&quot; to a Mage?&quot;). Will be added to the rewards list of all backers receiving the Contagion Chronicle PDF.</div>It seems pretty clear to me that at least part of the Player's Companion is supposed to address the mechanical interactions between the splats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T11:03:23-07:00","id":1301353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301345#post1301345\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seeping through. If you have a regular piece of paper, and a thick colored marker, when you draw on one side with the marker, sometimes it will bleed through, to the other. This is what's happening.</div> </div> </div> </div>I <b>know</b> what word Bleed mean in English - I do not know what does it mean <i>in context of Edinburgh setting</i>. What slips from where? What are symptoms of it? What is changed? Cause from my reading of previewed setting, Bleed is different symptom of Contagion than Blightfangers, super-mummy ( that just taken ride with it ) or the Grey 'antivirus'. <br /> <br /> Not too mention there was some infrormation of living becoming dead on masses, in Edinburgh introduction - and I do not see this in settings actual text.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T11:09:26-07:00","id":1301356,"title":"","content":"The subject of Death is <i>a lot of work</i> for something of a....well, niche concern. The vast majority of interactions comes down to &quot;It works like it would on anyone else&quot; or Clash of Wills. The stuff that came up in Princes of the Conquered Land is definitely interesting and useful, and even the subject of what player relationships might be built upon (Because <i>of course</i> one of those things a mummy/mage team up might consider is &quot;Hey, can you get my memory back?&quot;), but a lot of that plays second on the wider scale question of &quot;How to run these games together in a narrative sense that is cohesive and coherent&quot;-you start with the idea, form, the idioms, and the structure before you get down to the craft-and honestly the minutia is also the sort of thing that, if you enjoy the mystery setting of the game, might be better served by players just figuring out what happens at their own table.<br /> <br /> I mean, I get why people want it, I too want it, but I can also see why it's not quite the inherent part of the text that many people thought it would be. Fortunately, it got top priority in stretch goals.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T11:10:53-07:00","id":1301357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301353#post1301353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I <b>know</b> what word Bleed mean in English - I do not know what does it mean <i>in context of Edinburgh setting</i>. What slips from where? What are symptoms of it? What is changed? Cause from my reading of previewed setting, Bleed is different symptom of Contagion than Blightfangers, super-mummy ( that just taken ride with it ) or the Grey 'antivirus'.<br /> <br /> Not too mention there was some infrormation of living becoming dead on masses, in Edinburgh introduction - and I do not see this in settings actual text.</div> </div> </div> </div>Um, you were paying attention to the part on how the Grey manifests?<br /> <br /> It literally kills people in a week and it spreads via infected midges. That's pretty much the living becoming dead en masse. The Grey killed them, and the rising Contagion is making it worse to compensate.<br /> <br /> And we actually do have symptoms of Bleed. Iufenamun is one of them, and he's trying to make it worse to summon his manor from his native universe over. What his native universe is like is an exercise to the viewer, but it can be assumed a lot of the rumors sections are bits from his world crossing over into ours.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T11:11:28-07:00","id":1301358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301347#post1301347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That won't stop everyone from projecting the Crossover Chronicle they convinced themselves this would be onto Contagion and then being mad that it's not meeting that expectation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if I'm generally fine with idea of Contagion - I not agree that we (fans) 'convinced' <i>ourselves</i>. In 2016 book was announced as Crossover Chronicle. In 2017 OPP changed title to Contagion Chronicle, but still referencing crossover aspect of it. Now we are having fluff book about inter-factions relationships. I'm fine with it, but I'm one of the fans that looked exactly into development process for past 3 years. Most buyers just see 'in 2016 it was Crossover book, now it's not rules crossover - but with extra supplement from Stretch Goals - it will have crossover rules'. It looks... kinda not nice.<br /> <br /> Beside that, in general, Contagion idea is a bit confusing for even CoD fans. I did get questions on this on our Polish FB group, for example. People do not know if to treat it as universes 'system glitches', reality wars or supernatural disease...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 03-31-2019, 02:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T11:28:31-07:00","id":1301360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301358#post1301358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beside that, in general, Contagion idea is a bit confusing for even CoD fans. I did get questions on this on our Polish FB group, for example. People do not know if to treat it as universes 'system glitches', reality wars or supernatural disease...</div> </div> </div> </div>To which I say, once again:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tasti man LH</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1300683#post1300683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We've been doing this for, how many KSs now? Why are we still making absolute judgement calls on only pieces of the work without having the full work available for context?<br /> <br /> Calm down people.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://media.giphy.com/media/l0HlKrB02QY0f1mbm/giphy.gif\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div> </div> </div> </div>Also for the record, a past MMN gave an explanation on why the main book isn't nothing but rules:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We have received, over the years, many requests for crossover rules for the <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b>. Which makes sense, as <b>CofD</b>, unlike its predecessor, the <b>World of Darkness</b>, was created with the idea that all the game lines would have a similar, if not the same, rules set. I\u2019m not talking about the <i>Storyteller </i>and <i>Storytelling </i>Systems which are the rules for rolling dice, but the individual game line rules sets, like Disciplines, Gifts, cosmology, those sorts of things.<br /> <br /> With folks asking for crossover rules and tips, I suggested to our crew here that a crossover book would be something that could also be really helpful in providing new content for game lines that we were putting out less projects for that year.<br /> <br /> Pretty much the same thinking as the <b>Dark Eras</b> books.<br /> <br /> I wound up talking with Matthew Dawkins at the <i>Vampire </i>convention in New Orleans \u2013 the same one where we agreed on the deal for <b>They Came From Beneath the Sea!</b> \u2013 <b>and he made the point that a whoppin\u2019 book of pure rules with a bit of advice wouldn\u2019t necessarily be as much fun as a crossover book that featured a setting where those rules and that advice could be seen in action.</b><br /> <br /> <b>This tied in with my thinking on adding default Chronicles to each of the 2nd Edition CofD lines: provide an example that people could either use wholecloth or could take pieces of or just be inspired by for their own Chronicles.</b><br /> <br /> <b>Fun to read, and examples of how a Chronicle could work. So this crossover Chronicle would be the prime example of how to use all the various supernatural character types and their cultures in one big setting match up, usable as written and usable as examples and overall, no matter what, fun to read. </b><br /> <br /> Matthew went off and came up with an external threat; something not featured in any of our previous material, but which <i>could </i>be part of any of our <b>CofD </b>game lines. Something that threatened the supernatural world so much that the various denizens would have reasons to ally themselves \u2013 no matter how treacherously \u2013 to deal with it. And so the Contagion was born. </div> </div> </div><a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/achooo-hope-thats-contagious-monday-meeting-notes/\" target=\"_blank\">Source</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T11:30:13-07:00","id":1301361,"title":"","content":"This is why I commented early in the thread that the Introduction didn't quite capture the feel that Gentleman Gamer described in his Character Creation session: the Contagion is when things don't work the way that even the supposed experts think they should. It is by definition the ultimate \u201coutside the box\u201d experience; proof that the Chronicles of Darkness aren't just stranger than we know, but stranger than we <i>can</i> know. Is that \u201csystem glitches\u201d, reality wars, or supernatural disease? Yes. In particular, the more you try to pin it down as just one thing, the more you kill what it's supposed to be.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-31-2019, 02:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T11:32:25-07:00","id":1301362,"title":"","content":"I don\u2019t think the \u201cname was changed.\u201d It\u2019s kinda like how they don\u2019t reveal the full titles of game lines upon announcement - Demon the Frutang, Deviant the Blank. It\u2019s only later that the full title gets spoiled.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s really hard to claim a bait-and-switch on a three year old announcement of a project that, at that time, probably didn\u2019t have a finished outline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T11:37:53-07:00","id":1301364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>reseru</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301362#post1301362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don\u2019t think the \u201cname was changed.\u201d It\u2019s kinda like how they don\u2019t reveal the full titles of game lines upon announcement - Demon the Frutang, Deviant the Blank. It\u2019s only later that the full title gets spoiled.<br /> <br /> It\u2019s really hard to claim a bait-and-switch on a three year old announcement of a project that, at that time, probably didn\u2019t have a finished outline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, you mean it's not called Demon the Frutang?!<br /> <br /> HOW HAVE I BEEN MISREADING IT FOR ALL THESE YEARS?!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T12:19:40-07:00","id":1301367,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's all my fault <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In seriousness, it's impossible to write a book that covers a dozen game lines and pleases every kind of fan and roleplayer. I went with my best estimation for my outline of The Contagion Chronicle, and I stick by it. I still feel like an encyclopaedic book of how mage power x effects Promethean a like this and Promethean b like that would be dry and not appealing at all to the wider audience. After all, not everyone plays every single game. The Contagion Chronicle provides setting, playable factions, powers, new Conditions and Tilts, and chronicle hooks aplenty.<br /> <br /> I'm happy with the result.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":152,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","user":"The Gentleman Gamer","date":". 03-31-2019, 03:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":13}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T12:46:02-07:00","id":1301380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301358#post1301358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Beside that, in general, Contagion idea is a bit confusing for even CoD fans. I did get questions on this on our Polish FB group, for example. People do not know if to treat it as universes 'system glitches', reality wars or supernatural disease...</div> </div> </div> </div>It's supposed to be. When it shows up, things don't work the way they used to.<br /> <br /> Besides, from the two setting chapters, one can assume the manifestation of a strain isn't a random event; it needs something with profound symbolic weight of &quot;rebellion and malfunction&quot; before it finds a Patient Zero to poke through, and then at least a few symptoms echo the original host. Blightfangs, for instance, are drawn from their progenitor's own loneliness and need for a new family, ergo the disease spreads the condition she was accidentally given easily, while Knud wanted to keep ruling after the God-Machine tried to martyr him and broke his faith, so his Contagion manifests as turning people into easily swayed robots and also gives them a taste of losing faith in whatever made them happy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T12:57:36-07:00","id":1301384,"title":"","content":"Personally, I'm not the least bit interested in \u201chow does Discipline X intersect with Gift Y?\u201d The Crossover Crunch I'm more interested in is things like:<br /> <br /> \u2022 how do other splats cope with a Promethean's Disquiet?<br /> \u2022 what happens when a mage enters the Hedge? <br /> \u2022 the Argentum Transmutation is explicitly about crossovers; how does it apply to the various splats that aren't addressed in the Promethean core book?<br /> \u2022 which Arcana apply to each game's unique phenomena? <br /> \u2022 how do Hunter's vampires, werewolves, magicians, etc. relate to the Kindred, Uratha, Awakened, etc.<br /> <br /> Also, I'm hoping to see Bloodlines, Lodges, and Legacies that could only exist in a crossover context, because they're all about protagonists from game X actively engaging with phenomena from game Y.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T13:55:50-07:00","id":1301394,"title":"","content":"Those are the things I'm interested in seeing, I want to know if a demon's pledge to a changeling is tied to the cover or it's entire person.<br /> <br /> Or how a werewolf's harmony may be effected when in another invisible realm such as the underworld, astral, or hedge. I would imagine the half spirit being wouldn't feel right in places devoid of the Hisil.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T14:01:45-07:00","id":1301397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301348#post1301348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is literally everything we know about the \u201cDeath\u201d supplement so far:<br /> <div style=\"margin-left:40px\">At $55,000 in funding - CONTAGION CHRONICLE: PLAYER'S COMPANION - &amp;quot;Death&amp;quot; - A Player\u2019s Companion PDF supplement will be created for the Contagion Chronicle, containing a crunchy rules section on supernatural interactions with examples and guidance (ie, &amp;quot;What happens when a Vampire does &amp;quot;X&amp;quot; to a Mage?&amp;quot<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. Will be added to the rewards list of all backers receiving the Contagion Chronicle PDF.</div>It seems pretty clear to me that at least part of the Player's Companion is supposed to address the mechanical interactions between the splats.</div> </div> </div> </div>Should have specified I meant core contagion Chronicle book doesn't say it'll contain specific mechanical advice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25080-kargle18446","name":"Kargle18446","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T14:26:17-07:00","id":1301404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301384#post1301384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">how do other splats cope with a Promethean's Disquiet?</div> </div> </div> </div>I expect this will be covered in the Contagion core or in the AP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T14:38:34-07:00","id":1301410,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301367#post1301367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, it's all my fault <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> In seriousness, it's impossible to write a book that covers a dozen game lines and pleases every kind of fan and roleplayer. I went with my best estimation for my outline of The Contagion Chronicle, and I stick by it. I still feel like an encyclopaedic book of how mage power x effects Promethean a like this and Promethean b like that would be dry and not appealing at all to the wider audience. After all, not everyone plays every single game. The Contagion Chronicle provides setting, playable factions, powers, new Conditions and Tilts, and chronicle hooks aplenty.<br /> <br /> I'm happy with the result.</div> </div> </div> </div>What would you think of previewing the particular Conditions or Tilts that get mentioned in the different Setting Chapters? It would be nice to have the context as to what these things particularly do, since it seems like they're being used to express what the different iterations of the Contagion is capable of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T15:12:24-07:00","id":1301421,"title":"","content":"What I don't get is why there are so many reactions along the lines of \u201cwell, of <i>course</i> Contagion Chronicle doesn't have crossover crunch; you'd have to be ignorant to think otherwise,\u201d when the fact of the matter is that Contagion Chronicle <i>will</i> have crossover crunch, as many of us expected. That it's not in the main book but rather the companion isn't really a big deal, and in fact is probably better in the long term (as those of us who want crossover crunch but not Contagion can get the Companion without bothering with the main book that it's a companion to). But the point is that this <i>project</i> will be addressing crossover mechanics; and those of us who were expecting that weren't wrong. So please, no more of the \u201cit would be stupid to expect it\u201d remarks, OK?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T15:14:37-07:00","id":1301422,"title":"","content":"So did the God-Machine want Knud to die in the Cathedral or not? The text says both, at least twice each I think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25206-evil-midnight-lurker","name":"Evil Midnight Lurker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25206_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T15:24:30-07:00","id":1301427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301367#post1301367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The Contagion Chronicle provides setting, playable factions, powers, new Conditions and Tilts, and chronicle hooks aplenty.</div> </div> </div> </div>In all seriousness just adding in new powers that, presumably, every splat can access (on some level, etc.) makes a whole lot more sense than half a book of Clash of Wills redundancy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/638-reseru","name":"reseru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar638_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1574"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T15:26:36-07:00","id":1301429,"title":"","content":"And nobody was expecting half a book of Clash of Wills redundancy. That would be like the Spanish Inquisition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 03-31-2019, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T15:28:42-07:00","id":1301430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301421#post1301421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I don't get is why there are so many reactions along the lines of \u201cwell, of <i>course</i> Contagion Chronicle doesn't have crossover crunch</div> </div> </div> </div>Because it was never advertised to contain such, and there are other ongoing conversations (read: not here) where people are losing their shit because the game doesn't have what they expected it to simply because they assumed it would be a given - screeching over 'holding material hostage' as a stretch goal included.<br /> <br /> It's not personal and honestly, your responses have been far more sane and reasonable than the average for those that had other expectations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T15:44:51-07:00","id":1301435,"title":"","content":"For what it's worth, this is the only place that I'm following. So I was unaware of the vitriol elsewhere.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T15:47:27-07:00","id":1301437,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301435#post1301435\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For what it's worth, this is the only place that I'm following. So I was unaware of the vitriol elsewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Likewise. Sometimes, ignorance is bliss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T16:17:59-07:00","id":1301449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evil Midnight Lurker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301422#post1301422\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So did the God-Machine want Knud to die in the Cathedral or not? The text says both, at least twice each I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>'The God-Machine wanted this king to die in the cathedral and pass on the title, the land\u2019s faith changing, its will being done. Instead, he lived, died, and lived again.'<br /> <br /> What actually happened was he went into the cathedral, was killed, and his title was taken from him and he came back. The God Machine wanted him to die, it just didn't want him to die the way he did.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T16:20:14-07:00","id":1301450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301421#post1301421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I don't get is why there are so many reactions along the lines of \u201cwell, of <i>course</i> Contagion Chronicle doesn't have crossover crunch; you'd have to be ignorant to think otherwise,\u201d when the fact of the matter is that Contagion Chronicle <i>will</i> have crossover crunch, as many of us expected. That it's not in the main book but rather the companion isn't really a big deal, and in fact is probably better in the long term (as those of us who want crossover crunch but not Contagion can get the Companion without bothering with the main book that it's a companion to). But the point is that this <i>project</i> will be addressing crossover mechanics; and those of us who were expecting that weren't wrong. So please, no more of the \u201cit would be stupid to expect it\u201d remarks, OK?</div> </div> </div> </div>Mostly because it wasn't about crossover <i>mechanics,</i> it was about <i>crossover</i>. And, honestly, the bigger thread to a lot of making all of that is making the disparate threads of themes, moods, and languages work together than the mechanics.<br /> <br /> I've said it before, I'll say it again, &quot;fluff&quot; is harder than &quot;crunch&quot; (and I say that after, like, four months of panicking over crunch for Memento Mori, though other factors matter to the conversation). Making a satisfying crossover experience involves a lot of work in making the character choice of the player feel valid while blending them all into the same product, and that's <i>a shit ton of work</i>, one that needs tools.<br /> <br /> I'm surprised to see that it took Death to really get there, but as a craftsman, I'm not <i>that</i> surprised. The mechanics are much....lower on the list of things to get in order after getting the ideas and more fundamental elements of their execution onto the table, and books only have so much space-and really, the idea of the Contagion Chronicle is brilliant as a way of driving that home.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T16:29:45-07:00","id":1301454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301450#post1301450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mostly because it wasn't about crossover <i>mechanics,</i> it was about <i>crossover</i>. And, honestly, the bigger thread to a lot of making all of that is making the disparate threads of themes, moods, and languages work together than the mechanics.<br /> <br /> I've said it before, I'll say it again, &quot;fluff&quot; is harder than &quot;crunch&quot; (and I say that after, like, four months of panicking over crunch for Memento Mori, though other factors matter to the conversation). Making a satisfying crossover experience involves a lot of work in making the character choice of the player feel valid while blending them all into the same product, and that's <i>a shit ton of work</i>, one that needs tools.<br /> <br /> I'm surprised to see that it took Death to really get there, but as a craftsman, I'm not <i>that</i> surprised. The mechanics are much....lower on the list of things to get in order after getting the ideas and more fundamental elements of their execution onto the table, and books only have so much space-and really, the idea of the Contagion Chronicle is brilliant as a way of driving that home.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm actually experiencing this difficulty a bit for the Beast game I'm running. It's easy to just say &quot;Oh, there are werewolves over here, mages over here, vampires spread about doing their own thing...&quot; But working these different groups with differing themes into something that touches on the specific themes of Beast is... It's a bit more difficult!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T16:42:54-07:00","id":1301459,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301454#post1301454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm actually experiencing this difficulty a bit for the Beast game I'm running. It's easy to just say &quot;Oh, there are werewolves over here, mages over here, vampires spread about doing their own thing...&quot; But working these different groups with differing themes into something that touches on the specific themes of Beast is... It's a bit more difficult!</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the nice things is that Beast tends to be broad and simple all at once.<br /> <br /> But yeah, balancing the spiritualities and subsequent horrors, the body horrors on two and a half scales, the systemic horrors, human horrors, and political intrigue of two of them, the visceral on-the-field horror and excitement of two and how that differs from the third one, the dread seperation of two and the distant alienation of the third, so on and so forth-that's a lot to look at and manage, and none of that factors in how, despite it's breadth and simplicity, Beast <i>does</i> bring it's own things to a Vampire, Werewolf, and Mage discussion.<br /> <br /> One thing that's gonna get a thread here soon is Paris as a Crossover City and if people want that and how, because I'll be honest?<br /> <br /> I kind of feel like Paris as a Crossover City is a thing that should be done, but it's also <i>really hard to work out</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T16:47:31-07:00","id":1301464,"title":"","content":"Although I do have to say seeing some mummy stats was a interesting surprise. And I can't wait to see the conditions and tilts to see how the splats can or will be messed with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10820-blakemikizuki","name":"Blakemikizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10820_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"280"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T16:51:13-07:00","id":1301466,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301222#post1301222\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I believe that was planned for an upcoming book. Dave Brookshaw mentioned one Mage book having details regarding mage and host interaction.<br /> <br /> Might be one about putting normally antagonist folks in groups. Maybe some lost Sworn or False factions, or even Contagions that have 'won' and been excised from reality, leaving the survivors stuck in some hellhole outer world unable to escape.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds Wonderful! Hahahaahahahahahahhahahahahahahahaahhahahaahahhaah a<br /> <br /> Hoot hoot Vampires!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T17:13:04-07:00","id":1301470,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301449#post1301449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 'The God-Machine wanted this king to die in the cathedral and pass on the title, the land\u2019s faith changing, its will being done. Instead, he lived, died, and lived again.'<br /> <br /> What actually happened was he went into the cathedral, was killed, and his title was taken from him and he came back. The God Machine wanted him to die, it just didn't want him to die the way he did.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Denmark needed a strong leader in the times to come, where old gods and traditions slowly drowned in the mulch and were replaced by one omnipresent god and new ways of religious life. Knud was chosen as the guardian of Denmark. His power was to last for decades to ensure Odense\u2019s place on the map. Unexpected as it was, the murder of Knud marked the end of the Viking Age and ripped him away from his God-Machine ordained purpose as overseer and leader of a national part of Infrastructure. With his death, the Machine\u2019s plans were thrown into disarray.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25206-evil-midnight-lurker","name":"Evil Midnight Lurker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25206_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T17:23:44-07:00","id":1301472,"title":"","content":"Is the &quot;Athenaeum&quot; mentioned in the newest preview an area of the Underworld located near the Avernian Gate? I couldn't find that word in either Geist 1e or the Geist 2e back manuscript so I wasn't sure, but that's what it sounded like in context.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T17:26:13-07:00","id":1301473,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301410#post1301410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What would you think of previewing the particular Conditions or Tilts that get mentioned in the different Setting Chapters? It would be nice to have the context as to what these things particularly do, since it seems like they're being used to express what the different iterations of the Contagion is capable of.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'll post on Tuesday.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/22659-kickstarter-james","name":"Kickstarter James","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar22659_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T17:37:38-07:00","id":1301476,"title":"","content":"On the subject of a Contagion that has \u201cwon\u201d: has anyone considered the possibility that the Strix are one such example?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T17:41:52-07:00","id":1301477,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kickstarter James</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301473#post1301473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I'll post on Tuesday.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Really looking forward to it!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T17:48:42-07:00","id":1301480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Evil Midnight Lurker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301470#post1301470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unexpected as it was, the murder of Knud marked the end of the Viking Age and ripped him away from his God-Machine ordained purpose as overseer and leader of a national part of Infrastructure.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't believe this means actual overseer as much as a sort of spiritual one. It's possible that the God-Machine did mean for him to come back as a mentor figure, however (it would not be the first time the God Machine was involved in making a vampire), but the regicide and usurpation of his title kept that from happening.<br /> <br /> Remember the God Machine doesn't care about Knud specifically, it's trying to ease a conversion from paganism to Christianity. So in its ideal situation: Knud goes into a cathedral, prays, 'sees the light,' humbly hands over his titles to a just heir, and dies repentant. Centuries later, people are wearing What Would Knud Do bracelets and honoring his memory. Sometimes they might claim to have seen his ghost nodding to them before they did a good deed.<br /> <br /> Instead: Knud goes into a cathedral, gets betrayed (not normally seen as a good thing to be rewarded in Christianity), murdered in a sanctuary, and the folks who did it get to be the king now. Over the course of centuries, when Knud is seen, it's as a scary thing, a 'horrifying blood-sucking monster,' who often haunts the grounds of the holy space he reached for sanctuary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-31-2019, 09:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T18:01:52-07:00","id":1301482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301450#post1301450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mostly because it wasn't about crossover <i>mechanics,</i> it was about <i>crossover</i>. And, honestly, the bigger thread to a lot of making all of that is making the disparate threads of themes, moods, and languages work together than the mechanics.<br /> <br /> I've said it before, I'll say it again, &amp;quot;fluff&amp;quot; is harder than &amp;quot;crunch&amp;quot; (and I say that after, like, four months of panicking over crunch for Memento Mori, though other factors matter to the conversation). Making a satisfying crossover experience involves a lot of work in making the character choice of the player feel valid while blending them all into the same product, and that's <i>a shit ton of work</i>, one that needs tools.<br /> <br /> I'm surprised to see that it took Death to really get there, but as a craftsman, I'm not <i>that</i> surprised. The mechanics are much....lower on the list of things to get in order after getting the ideas and more fundamental elements of their execution onto the table, and books only have so much space-and really, the idea of the Contagion Chronicle is brilliant as a way of driving that home.</div> </div> </div> </div>For what it's worth, I've never advocated for the book being <i>just</i> about the mechanics; I've always viewed them as a small but essential part of the issue. But just as I wouldn't want the book too be all about crossover crunch, I also wouldn't want it to be completely devoid of it; there are some crunch issues that just have to be addressed, at least in a general sense. <br /> <br /> All that said, I'm fine with crossover fluff getting top billing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T18:27:43-07:00","id":1301486,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Minty</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301472#post1301472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the &quot;Athenaeum&quot; mentioned in the newest preview an area of the Underworld located near the Avernian Gate? I couldn't find that word in either Geist 1e or the Geist 2e back manuscript so I wasn't sure, but that's what it sounded like in context.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Try the Book of the Dead; the Athenaeum is the Dominion that serves as a library of lost knowledge. It's in the 2E core under a different name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T19:22:01-07:00","id":1301490,"title":"","content":"Just mentioned this elsewhere but it seems like the Contagion scenario could be the reason for the rise of Lycaon-Ur and his Lodge of the Field in Poland. Just coincidental, I'm sure, since werewolves tend to change and warp a lot even without the interference of other worlds. Milo just pointed out the situation in Dubai too.<br /> <br /> Either way I'm liking these 'bosses' and hoping there's a werewolf one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-31-2019, 10:25 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T21:15:05-07:00","id":1301501,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301486#post1301486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Try the Book of the Dead; the Athenaeum is the Dominion that serves as a library of lost knowledge. It's in the 2E core under a different name.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T22:44:29-07:00","id":1301521,"title":"","content":"On Odense setting - A little nitpick. Preview states: 'Crowned during the transition period from Viking Age to the early Middle Ages.' The thing is that Vikings Era WAS Early Middle Ages. <br /> <br /> Like Wolf &amp; Raven Dark Era points, Vikings where in years circa 700-1100 - after this period we have 'proper', High Middle Ages - with large castles, great nobility and Crusades. So Odense should probably point that Knuds crowning ends in high Middle Ages. Especially, as Knud is mentioned to partake in Crusades himself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-01-2019, 01:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-03-31T23:42:53-07:00","id":1301534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301490#post1301490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just mentioned this elsewhere but it seems like the Contagion scenario could be the reason for the rise of Lycaon-Ur and his Lodge of the Field in Poland. Just coincidental, I'm sure, since werewolves tend to change and warp a lot even without the interference of other worlds. Milo just pointed out the situation in Dubai too.<br /> <br /> Either way I'm liking these 'bosses' and hoping there's a werewolf one.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well there's 12 settings and 11 splats (including Deviant) so hopefully we'll see one for each.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25080-kargle18446","name":"Kargle18446","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T00:26:20-07:00","id":1301541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301480#post1301480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't believe this means actual overseer as much as a sort of spiritual one. It's possible that the God-Machine did mean for him to come back as a mentor figure, however (it would not be the first time the God Machine was involved in making a vampire), but the regicide and usurpation of his title kept that from happening.<br /> <br /> Remember the God Machine doesn't care about Knud specifically, it's trying to ease a conversion from paganism to Christianity. So in its ideal situation: Knud goes into a cathedral, prays, 'sees the light,' humbly hands over his titles to a just heir, and dies repentant. Centuries later, people are wearing What Would Knud Do bracelets and honoring his memory. Sometimes they might claim to have seen his ghost nodding to them before they did a good deed.<br /> <br /> Instead: Knud goes into a cathedral, gets betrayed (not normally seen as a good thing to be rewarded in Christianity), murdered in a sanctuary, and the folks who did it get to be the king now. Over the course of centuries, when Knud is seen, it's as a scary thing, a 'horrifying blood-sucking monster,' who often haunts the grounds of the holy space he reached for sanctuary.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, that seems reasonable, I can wrap my head around it now. Thanks!<br /> <br /> ...moving forward, it seems simultaneously weird and reasonable to me that Kyoto is a focus city instead of Tokyo. I mean, Tokyo is the city where all the splats hang out already... but dumping the Contagion on it would be kind of disruptive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25206-evil-midnight-lurker","name":"Evil Midnight Lurker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25206_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T02:18:09-07:00","id":1301555,"title":"","content":"I say that Odense write-up finally 'get me' with Contagion. It seems much more 'we connect setting to history of area' than Edinburgh's 'here's three different Contagions - do something about it as ST'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-01-2019, 05:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T02:56:12-07:00","id":1301559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301555#post1301555\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I say that Odense write-up finally 'get me' with Contagion. It seems much more 'we connect setting to history of area' than Edinburgh's 'here's three different Contagions - do something about it ST'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fun fact about the Edinburgh setting; Knud gets name dropped as the sire for our original Blightfang. It evolved into that new form, which is nice to see. The Contagion changes, adapts...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T03:52:44-07:00","id":1301568,"title":"","content":"So I have a query I was hoping some of you guys could weigh in on. <br /> <br /> So in the Odense preview the Contagion is described as manifesting in &quot;Mortals&quot; as the Hallowed condition, but then goes on to say in the story hooks section that Mages, most prominently, but also Prometheans and Mummy's can be effected by it as well, which is confusing as certainly the latter is the opposite of &quot;mortal&quot;, but there's no reference to the contagion producing a different effect in anything but Vampires. <br /> <br /> Additionally the Edinburgh preview confuses things further by saying the Grey doesn't effect supernatural creatures in the same way as &quot;Mortals&quot;, suggesting anything supernatural is not considered a &quot;mortal&quot; which is contradictory to what I just pointed out in the Odense preview.<br /> <br /> So is this just a case of my misreading or does anyone else agree that defining the contagions victims by the &quot;Mortal&quot; tag is a potentially confusing issue?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25080-kargle18446","name":"Kargle18446","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T04:38:22-07:00","id":1301576,"title":"","content":"If considering these settings as rules to play by then certainly it is confusing. But as ideas and inspiration, it shows that different contagions can have different targets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24020-mateus","name":"Mateus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24020_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"55"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T04:50:41-07:00","id":1301579,"title":"","content":"I'd expect any remaining inconsistencies to get picked up during the editing and development stages and cleared up there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T05:02:23-07:00","id":1301582,"title":"","content":"The Contagion manifests in different ways in different settings. In some places it only hits mortals, in others it only hits werewolves, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T05:45:40-07:00","id":1301589,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301582#post1301582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Contagion manifests in different ways in different settings. In some places it only hits mortals, in others it only hits werewolves, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Would it be possible to clarify if in Odense the Contagion hits just non-supernatural mortals with the Hollowing Condition or if it effects all non-vampires with it?<br /> <br /> For me it's more that what beings are defined as &quot;Mortals&quot; seems to have changed between the two settings that's a confusing issue rather than the fact that the Contagion can effect different beings (which I do really like.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25080-kargle18446","name":"Kargle18446","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T06:14:33-07:00","id":1301598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kargle18446</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301589#post1301589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Would it be possible to clarify if in Odense the Contagion hits just non-supernatural mortals with the Hollowing Condition or if it effects all non-vampires with it?<br /> <br /> For me it's more that what beings are defined as &quot;Mortals&quot; seems to have changed between the two settings that's a confusing issue rather than the fact that the Contagion can effect different beings (which I do really like.)</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In Odense it's hit mortals more than anyone else because they have contact with the infected relics. However, it can transmit to other creatures too. I'll ensure it's clear in the finished text. The Hollowed Condition does not discriminate in its targets.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T06:24:48-07:00","id":1301602,"title":"","content":"Can beast or changelig be hit by Hollowed, like depression symptoms? They are mentioned as most affected by Contagion - and their race specifics made them most connected to mortal population at large.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T06:33:08-07:00","id":1301604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301598#post1301598\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> In Odense it's hit mortals more than anyone else because they have contact with the infected relics. However, it can transmit to other creatures too. I'll ensure it's clear in the finished text. The Hollowed Condition does not discriminate in its targets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, that's great to know. Makes investigating that Contagion a whole lot more sinister when your at risk of contracting it as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25080-kargle18446","name":"Kargle18446","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T06:38:03-07:00","id":1301606,"titl