ollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>I love idea of this cross-splats powers! </b>I may have a bit bum on specifics off Specializations, but concept, on general, is great.<br /> <br /> <b>Now the question is will we have more powers per Sworn / False groups?</b> I assume whole Authority Vector is <b>not</b> <i>only</i> Surveillance power, correct?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just add to what someone else said we know that each of the Sworn have their own Vectors. Not sure about false as vectors weren't mentioned on their summary pages but the vector chapter description includes them so I assume they get something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25080-kargle18446","name":"Kargle18446","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T10:14:36-07:00","id":1301672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kargle18446</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301668#post1301668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just add to what someone else said we know that each of the Sworn have their own Vectors. Not sure about false as vectors weren't mentioned on their summary pages but the vector chapter description includes them so I assume they get something.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh, they get something...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T10:20:58-07:00","id":1301675,"title":"","content":"One question that sticks with me: why the mechanics that require specific multiple numbers of successes (such as resisting Iufenamen's memory drain, or using Surveillance on more secure systems)? Is this a deliberate deviation from the mechanics common to all the individual gamelines, where difficulty is by default modeled with dice penalties rather than granular successes? Like how Mummy deviates in that it's the one gameline where magic fiddles with the rolled target number?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T10:37:56-07:00","id":1301686,"title":"","content":"So here is my question (which we'll find out the answer to tomorrow I presume): are Edges something that only apply to the Cryptocrat of that splat, are they purchased or apply automatically, or do they apply to every Sworn in the group? <br /> <br /> I'm assuming for now that apply automatically and that if you have a group of Sworn containing Beast, a Demon, a Vampire, and Hunter everyone will automatically gain access to all four Edges (at this dot at least) since one of the selling points of Contagion is that groups get more powerful as they get more diverse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T19:13:31-07:00","id":1301784,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kargle18446</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301668#post1301668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just add to what someone else said we know that each of the Sworn have their own Vectors. Not sure about false as vectors weren't mentioned on their summary pages but the vector chapter description includes them so I assume they get something.</div> </div> </div> </div> All the False get the Contagion Vector.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T19:47:06-07:00","id":1301788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301602#post1301602\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can beast or changelig be hit by Hollowed, like depression symptoms? They are mentioned as most affected by Contagion - and their race specifics made them most connected to mortal population at large.</div> </div> </div> </div> Most religions are living in the sense of having someone trying to continue such traditions or recreate them or simply inspired by them. <br /> <br /> I worship Gods like Hephaestus, Flora, and Bastet, but I don't make it a thing when they are depicted in fiction, even in ways that are not flattering, such as Scion depicting Bastet as a drunk (which is very much not how I view her). Acting as muses is one of the gifts that Gods (and saints and angels) gives to humanity. <br /> <br /> As for why the Godmachine seems to prefer Abrahamic religions, I think it has more to do with discouraging Gnostism then promoting Abrahamic religions. Both Gnostism and even Neoplatonism leads too many questions about Demiurges, it'd rather one just be do as they are told or failing that be Atheist. <br /> <br /> As for Paganism and the Godmachine, there really hasn't been much if any exploration of what Godmachine Archangels are, and could they be parts of the Godmachine with different agendas. Perhaps that Godmachine isn't as unified as appearances suggest. <br /> <br /> Sometimes the Godmachine is the bad guy and some times the good guy, and sometimes all that is holding a part of the world together at all. <br /> <br /> One thing I hope the book discusses is the relationship of all the none demon splats to the Godmachine as A-side from the Contagion it seems the most frequent thing the Sworn and False run up against.<br /> <br /> Oops qouted the wrong person, my bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T19:55:42-07:00","id":1301792,"title":"","content":"Can a Bound's Geist use it's Vectors?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T20:02:54-07:00","id":1301793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301788#post1301788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Most religions are living in the sense of having someone trying to continue such traditions or recreate them or simply inspired by them.<br /> <br /> I worship Gods like Hephaestus, Flora, and Bastet, but I don't make it a thing when they are depicted in fiction, even in ways that are not flattering, such as Scion depicting Bastet as a drunk (which is very much not how I view her). Acting as muses is one of the gifts that Gods (and saints and angels) gives to humanity.<br /> <br /> As for why the Godmachine seems to prefer Abrahamic religions, I think it has more to do with discouraging Gnostism then promoting Abrahamic religions. Both Gnostism and even Neoplatonism leads too many questions about Demiurges, it'd rather one just be do as they are told or failing that be Atheist.<br /> <br /> As for Paganism and the Godmachine, there really hasn't been much if any exploration of what Godmachine Archangels are, and could they be parts of the Godmachine with different agendas. Perhaps that Godmachine isn't as unified as appearances suggest.<br /> <br /> Sometimes the Godmachine is the bad guy and some times the good guy, and sometimes all that is holding a part of the world together at all.<br /> <br /> One thing I hope the book discusses is the relationship of all the none demon splats to the Godmachine as A-side from the Contagion it seems the most frequent thing the Sworn and False run up against.<br /> <br /> Oops qouted the wrong person, my bad.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I would like to add to this:<br /> <br /> It also gives King Knud the cache of being betrayed by God, and from there rising from the grave as the instrument of his own revenge.<br /> <br /> He's Danish Coppola Dracula. Probably kind of acts like him too, if he's trying to shake off the Contagious ennui.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T20:22:16-07:00","id":1301795,"title":"","content":"I'm looking forward to a m