00,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301797#post1301797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Looks like it.<br /> <br /> \u201cMe\u00f0 konungr munu land standa\u201d (With king shall land stand)<br /> <br /> If one wanted 'more' from him in a campaign (though he seems like enough of a threat as is, especially given however many childer you give him) you could probably easily attach some land controlling abilities, in addition to his people-controlling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fisher Kings are always fun!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-01T20:47:25-07:00","id":1301801,"title":"","content":"I keep thinking of Faethor Ferenczy from the Necroscope series, who had enough control over the descendants of his servants from when he was a noble hundreds of years later that he could get them to commit suicide en masse. Even given the events, presumably some of Knud's followers were loyal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-01-2019, 11:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T07:55:14-07:00","id":1301907,"title":"","content":"Backers now have whole Vectors chapter and Condition and Tilts Appendix - so we can see how Contagion WORKS and how Sworn and False are fighting it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T08:36:30-07:00","id":1301918,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301788#post1301788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Most religions are living in the sense of having someone trying to continue such traditions or recreate them or simply inspired by them.<br /> <br /> I worship Gods like Hephaestus, Flora, and Bastet, but I don't make it a thing when they are depicted in fiction, even in ways that are not flattering, such as Scion depicting Bastet as a drunk (which is very much not how I view her). Acting as muses is one of the gifts that Gods (and saints and angels) gives to humanity.<br /> <br /> As for why the Godmachine seems to prefer Abrahamic religions, I think it has more to do with discouraging Gnostism then promoting Abrahamic religions. Both Gnostism and even Neoplatonism leads too many questions about Demiurges, it'd rather one just be do as they are told or failing that be Atheist.<br /> <br /> As for Paganism and the Godmachine, there really hasn't been much if any exploration of what Godmachine Archangels are, and could they be parts of the Godmachine with different agendas. Perhaps that Godmachine isn't as unified as appearances suggest.<br /> <br /> Sometimes the Godmachine is the bad guy and some times the good guy, and sometimes all that is holding a part of the world together at all.<br /> <br /> One thing I hope the book discusses is the relationship of all the none demon splats to the Godmachine as A-side from the Contagion it seems the most frequent thing the Sworn and False run up against.<br /> <br /> Oops qouted the wrong person, my bad.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Good point about living vs. non-living religions. I think there's a different theology behind your worship of gods like Hephaestus, Flora, and Bastet and the Catholic view of saints, but I could be wrong. Regardless, I'm simply expressing my own personal discomfort with this particular plot point. I'm pledged to the Kickstarter and have no intentions of changing that, so I don't think I'm making too much of a big deal out of it. <br /> <br /> I like your idea of the God-Machine liking Abrahamic religions because of their opposition to Gnosticism given the way that melds with Mage: The Awakening. That said, I'm not sure the God-Machine does favor Abrahamic religions, except in particular places for its own inscrutable purposes. The wonder of Chronicles of Darkness, of course, is the room it leaves for personal interpretation. I tend to see the God-Machine as meddlesome Cthulhu, not particularly concerned about human worship or even whether or not human beings are intentionally obeying or disobeying so long as it is able to further its purposes. But as I said, that's just personal interpretation. <br /> <br /> I do think you're right that the God Machine seems to be threaded throughout the Contagion Chronicles. I think your idea of it discussing non-Demon splats relationship to the God-Machine is good, though if they do I hope they do a Blasphemies-style suite of options for each Splat rather than a single overarching old World of Darkness style answer. I prefer things being a little open to interpretation.<br /> <br /> To be honest, one of the things that worries me a bit about the Chronicle so far is how big of a role the God-Machine is playing. I'll have to wait for the final product, of course, but the danger with the God-Machine is that its themes can seem to override any other splats cosmology and themes unless handled well. I have some concern that we could end up with this basically being a Demon Chronicle with other supporting cast rather than its own thing.<br /> <br /> Or, alternatively, shaping up to be a kind of Chronicles of Darkness version of Werewolf: The Apocalypse's Triat, with the Contagion being the Wyrm and the God-Machine being the Weaver (not sure who the Wyld would be though). <br /> <br /> But we'll see.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25193-ethawyn","name":"ethawyn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T09:03:42-07:00","id":1301921,"title":"","content":"Some more previews some more questions xD <br /> <br /> So I was under the impression that the Blightfang was spread by bloodline of Vampires that originated with Maggie and caused regular humans who were bitten to develop a pseudo-vampirism. However the appendix condition states that Beast's and Ghosts and other supernatural predators can spread it (which is awesome) but makes me wonder about the conditions of infection. <br /> <br /> Would I be correct in thinking supernatural creatures can catch it from either infected supernatural predators or from hanging out near infected bodies while mortals can additionally catch it from other infected mortals? Additionally would infected supernaturals suffer from the pseudo-vampirism or is that just mortals?<br /> <br /> As a separate point the Grey infection explicitly does not kill supernatural creatures but does physically mark them (at least it does vampires). However the Grey condition profile make no mention of this aspect of it, is this an oversight or a case of the reader having to make the conclusion themselves?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25080-kargle18446","name":"Kargle18446","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T09:12:23-07:00","id":1301923,"title":"","content":"Mummy fans: consider this:<br /> A Mummy using the Blessed is the God-King Utterance in addition with the Godhead Vector","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T10:13:10-07:00","id":1301941,"title":"","content":"Thinks there's a problem for on one of the powers that seems more like a negative than positive for vectors<br /> <br /> Beasts: A Beast using Drain Energy raises her Satiety to 10. pg 50 second manuscript for vector","signature":"","edited":{"userid":893,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","user":"reaperfrost8","date":". 04-02-2019, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T10:16:43-07:00","id":1301943,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kargle18446</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301921#post1301921\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some more previews some more questions xD<br /> <br /> So I was under the impression that the Blightfang was spread by bloodline of Vampires that originated with Maggie and caused regular humans who were bitten to develop a pseudo-vampirism. However the appendix condition states that Beast's and Ghosts and other supernatural predators can spread it (which is awesome) but makes me wonder about the conditions of infection.<br /> <br /> Would I be correct in thinking supernatural creatures can catch it from either infected supernatural predators or from hanging out near infected bodies while mortals can additionally catch it from other infected mortals? Additionally would infected supernaturals suffer from the pseudo-vampirism or is that just mortals?<br /> <br /> As a separate point the Grey infection explicitly does not kill supernatural creatures but does physically mark them (at least it does vampires). However the Grey condition profile make no mention of this aspect of it, is this an oversight or a case of the reader having to make the conclusion themselves?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Vague on the just mortals or not, but by the looks of it, the IMMA VAMPIRAH symptom can easily be IMMA GHOAST, IMMA BEGAHTTAN or even IMMA CHAEHGELING, beyond the light allergy. And leads to the rather hilarious image of a rather befuddled Lost being followed around by crooning servants who seem absolutely convinced they're hobgoblins after she did a rather wide-ranging Harvest.<br /> <br /> Also, wow. The Contagion Vector is horrifying, and yet, something that sounds completely reasonable to have, even to the Crucible Initiative. I like how the Fire-Bearers are also the only ones who have Specializations that allow them to buff other people, because they're not so much False nihilists as extremist Sworn. On a related note, I like how learning it is less of mutual maturation of the False cell and far more competitive in nature; the False are in it for themselves, and that doesn't really lend itself to the power of friendship, no matter how useful it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T10:25:31-07:00","id":1301946,"title":"","content":"I'm not far in Vectors, but I've got <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=I8GVzyU6fcY\" target=\"_blank\">Play With Fire </a>going for them. This is good stuff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T10:47:31-07:00","id":1301947,"title":"","content":"I hope my compiled citation from Vector chapter is not too much, but it shows how Sworn are generally split over all of monsters ( and hunters ) factions in CoD universe - showing more on the idea what follows around them.<ul><li>Cryptocrats \u2013 Authority Vector \u2013 Typical members are: beasts, demons, mages and vampires. Joins them Winter Court, Cheiron Group, Task Force: Valkyrie, Maa-Kep, and Undertakers from Sin-Eaters.</li> <li>Jeremiad \u2013 Frevor Vector \u2013 Typical members are: beasts, hunters, mummies and Prometheans. Joins them Integrators, Lancea et Sanctum, Long Night, Lucifuge, and Malleus Maleficarum</li> <li>Rosetta Society \u2013 Semiotics Vector \u2013 Typical members are: mage, demons, changelings, hunters and werewolves. Joins too them Circle of the Crone, Sesha-Hebsu, Mourners from Sin-Eaters and Tammuz.</li> <li>Ship of Theseus \u2013 Realignment Vector \u2013 Typical members are: Prometheans, demons and Sin-Eaters. Joins to them Free Council, Carthian Movement, Ordo Dracul, Iron Masters, Spring Court and Network Zero.</li> <li>Zero Hour \u2013 Intel Vector \u2013 Typical members are: Forsaken werewolves, hunters, Deviants \u2013 and members of Adamantine Arrow, Saboteurs, and Furies from Sin-Eaters.</li> </ul>Interesting to me are Undertakers in Cryptocrats, Mourners and Tammuz in Rosetta - or why there are only pointed Forsaken in Zero Hour, not whole Uratha race?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-02-2019, 01:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T11:27:28-07:00","id":1301957,"title":"","content":"Probably because the stereotypical Sworn is considerably more altruistic that the stereotypical Pure. Like, I'm sure that there plenty of Pure in Zero Hour, but those are exceptional or notable members, not typical members.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T11:30:18-07:00","id":1301958,"title":"","content":"Tammuz are in Rosetta because language is part of their creation, like the Golem of Prague. (Or the golem in The Order for that matter.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8719-florin","name":"Florin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"940"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T11:42:31-07:00","id":1301961,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Florin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301958#post1301958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Tammuz are in Rosetta because language is part of their creation, like the Golem of Prague. (Or the golem in The Order for that matter.)</div> </div> </div> </div>This would mean that Galateids should also be in Rosetta, as they are Generated with 'Breath of Life' - What is more like 'symbology in action' then?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T12:03:09-07:00","id":1301968,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301961#post1301961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This would mean that Galateids should also be in Rosetta, as they are Generated with 'Breath of Life' - What is more like 'symbology in action' then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Breath of life is not language, it was blessing of the Gods in the original myth. The golem was directly animated by sacred words.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T12:06:09-07:00","id":1301970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301943#post1301943\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Vague on the just mortals or not, but by the looks of it, the IMMA VAMPIRAH symptom can easily be IMMA GHOAST, IMMA BEGAHTTAN or even IMMA CHAEHGELING, beyond the light allergy. And leads to the rather hilarious image of a rather befuddled Lost being followed around by crooning servants who seem absolutely convinced they're hobgoblins after she did a rather wide-ranging Harvest.<br /> <br /> Also, wow. The Contagion Vector is horrifying, and yet, something that sounds completely reasonable to have, even to the Crucible Initiative. I like how the Fire-Bearers are also the only ones who have Specializations that allow them to buff other people, because they're not so much False nihilists as extremist Sworn. On a related note, I like how learning it is less of mutual maturation of the False cell and far more competitive in nature; the False are in it for themselves, and that doesn't really lend itself to the power of friendship, no matter how useful it is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it says their urged to perform the &quot;same self-sustaining task&quot; so I imagine feeding wise they try to propagate those emotions that were fed off in others. How far that dillusion spreads with splats other than vampires could be pretty entertaining though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25080-kargle18446","name":"Kargle18446","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T12:38:54-07:00","id":1301973,"title":"","content":"While the Contagion Vector is horrifying and the Fervor Vector is awesomely over the top..<br /> <br /> Realignment is amazing, especially Evolve. The possibilities are hilarious to consider","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T12:40:33-07:00","id":1301975,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kargle18446</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301970#post1301970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well it says their urged to perform the &amp;quot;same self-sustaining task&amp;quot; so I imagine feeding wise they try to propagate those emotions that were fed off in others. How far that dillusion spreads with splats other than vampires could be pretty entertaining though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Precisely. I can see a bunch of Lost Blightfangs, infected by the Winter Court, surruptiously surrounding a house, and then, when the inhabitants are all unnerved, spontaneously breaking out into a chorus of Linkin Park.<br /> <br /> The best part is, if the inhabitants start laughing their asses off, the Blightfangs think they've got some good enough Glamour and slink off. It's the kind of thing most mortals think is a bunch of pranksters and only noticable if you know what Blightfang is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T12:46:53-07:00","id":1301976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301968#post1301968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Breath of life is not language, it was blessing of the Gods in the original myth. The golem was directly animated by sacred words.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not just that. In Promethean 2e, the Tammuz have a connection to language: one of their Bestowments is Inscription, and people infected by a Tammuz' Disquiet tend to babel. It very much makes sense for the Tammuz to have a special facility with the Semiotics Vector.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 04-02-2019, 03:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T12:50:58-07:00","id":1301978,"title":"","content":"I hope There\u2019s a mention of the Decived!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T12:52:46-07:00","id":1301980,"title":"","content":"The Beast Edge for Drain Energy in the Contagion Vector might want to be looked at. Having your Satiety skyrocket to 10 isn't as good of a thing for Beasts as refilling Aether for Demons or Glamour for Changeling is.<br /> <br /> As it is, I'm not sure why a False Beast would want to slap themselves with the Slumbering Condition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T13:09:37-07:00","id":1301987,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301975#post1301975\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Precisely. I can see a bunch of Lost Blightfangs, infected by the Winter Court, surruptiously surrounding a house, and then, when the inhabitants are all unnerved, spontaneously breaking out into a chorus of Linkin Park.<br /> <br /> The best part is, if the inhabitants start laughing their asses off, the Blightfangs think they've got some good enough Glamour and slink off. It's the kind of thing most mortals think is a bunch of pranksters and only noticable if you know what Blightfang is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Makes me wonder what a ghost inflicted Blightfang would do to try to feed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25080-kargle18446","name":"Kargle18446","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T13:14:59-07:00","id":1301990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301976#post1301976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's not just that. In Promethean 2e, the Tammuz have a connection to language: one of their Bestowments is Inscription, and people infected by a Tammuz' Disquiet tend to babel. It very much makes sense for the Tammuz to have a special facility with the Semiotics Vector.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally forgot that, but yes!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T13:21:30-07:00","id":1301993,"title":"","content":"Shouldn't the Mage Edge for Intel Vector *** Fire for Effect also include Unraveling spells along with Fraying and Unmaking?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T13:21:37-07:00","id":1301994,"title":"","content":"Under Resolution for the Reality Bleed Tilt it says &quot;the Factions have vectors designed for repairing reality;&quot;<br /> I must be blind because I can't find anything regarding repairing reality in the Vectors chapter.<br /> <br /> I will say, though, that all of the Vectors themselves look really cool, both in terms of mechanics and fluff, and even have mechanics that support and inform fluff. They definitely make me feel like playing a crossover game more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12738,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","user":"Minty","date":". 04-02-2019, 04:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T14:26:11-07:00","id":1302011,"title":"","content":"Yeah, also the Godhead Vector costs way too much, and has a wonky Duration; it's one Willpower or two lethal damage per turn to maintain, when a lot of its powers cost Willpower and assuming it costs three, and it's said to last a scene when it can explicitly lapse if keeping it up gets too tiring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T15:15:55-07:00","id":1302022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301980#post1301980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Beast Edge for Drain Energy in the Contagion Vector might want to be looked at. Having your Satiety skyrocket to 10 isn't as good of a thing for Beasts as refilling Aether for Demons or Glamour for Changeling is.<br /> <br /> As it is, I'm not sure why a False Beast would want to slap themselves with the Slumbering Condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>This would work fine if it specified that the Beast only took the Gorged Condition instead of Slumbering.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T15:19:27-07:00","id":1302024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301788#post1301788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Most religions are living in the sense of having someone trying to continue such traditions or recreate them or simply inspired by them.<br /> <br /> I worship Gods like Hephaestus, Flora, and Bastet, but I don't make it a thing when they are depicted in fiction, even in ways that are not flattering, such as Scion depicting Bastet as a drunk (which is very much not how I view her). Acting as muses is one of the gifts that Gods (and saints and angels) gives to humanity.<br /> <br /> As for why the Godmachine seems to prefer Abrahamic religions, I think it has more to do with discouraging Gnostism then promoting Abrahamic religions. Both Gnostism and even Neoplatonism leads too many questions about Demiurges, it'd rather one just be do as they are told or failing that be Atheist.<br /> <br /> As for Paganism and the Godmachine, there really hasn't been much if any exploration of what Godmachine Archangels are, and could they be parts of the Godmachine with different agendas. Perhaps that Godmachine isn't as unified as appearances suggest.<br /> <br /> Sometimes the Godmachine is the bad guy and some times the good guy, and sometimes all that is holding a part of the world together at all.<br /> <br /> One thing I hope the book discusses is the relationship of all the none demon splats to the Godmachine as A-side from the Contagion it seems the most frequent thing the Sworn and False run up against.<br /> <br /> Oops qouted the wrong person, my bad.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I see no contradiction in God's Machine angels having conflicts with each other, if they keep legalistic, they basically obey a primary schedule, rather than a beehive mind or being led by God Machine. Any principle may conflict with another, just as any primary programming may conflict with another, sometimes it may even be intentional to generate evolution by selecting the most efficient programming.<br /> <br /> This may include paganism. And even to solve the contradictions of the Machine God to want two contradictory things at the same time.<br /> <br /> I really do find it strange that Buddhism is so little approached in Demon. The God Machine has several attributes of Mara.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/641-ben-linus","name":"Ben Linus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"444"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T15:29:13-07:00","id":1302027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1302022#post1302022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This would work fine if it specified that the Beast only took the Gorged Condition instead of Slumbering.</div> </div> </div> </div>Precisely. That'd show the maximum potential power while still allowing them to actually use it. Just needs to be explicit.<br /> <br /> Also, yeah, I once called the Contagion Warhammer Chaos. I'd like to revise that to Glorantha Chaos with Warhammer aesthetics. Particularly given how those who willingly use it in its most terrible form have, as a near basic power, <i>reducing </i>their internal corruption (by putting it in someone else, but hey, who's counting?). I'd have to see the Contagious as a whole to solidify, but given how the end state of the Geryo strain seems to be &quot;your mutations take control of you and you become a savage, many-limbed monster that calls back to something that Father Wolf himself spurned as too bloodthirsty to be noble warriors,&quot; I'm not expecting to be all that wrong.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Speaking of, what does a Geryo do once it's fully born? By the looks of it, they regain their shapeshifting, but do they get a mind and social attributes back?<br /> <br /> I will note that King Knud seems to have an Integrity score (which is likely a misprint), though; his strain doesn't seem to have obliterated his humanity, given how he acts like a normal elder a lot of the time. I'm guessing not all Contagious are unplayable, just most of them (the end state of Blightfang, I'll bet, for mortals, if they have an actual Contagion and not simply victims of their &quot;master's&quot; infection).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":180,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","user":"Leliel","date":". 04-02-2019, 06:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T15:31:17-07:00","id":1302028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ben Linus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1302024#post1302024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I see no contradiction in God's Machine angels having conflicts with each other, if they keep legalistic, they basically obey a primary schedule, rather than a beehive mind or being led by God Machine. Any principle may conflict with another, just as any primary programming may conflict with another, sometimes it may even be intentional to generate evolution by selecting the most efficient programming.<br /> <br /> This may include paganism. And even to solve the contradictions of the Machine God to want two contradictory things at the same time.<br /> <br /> I really do find it strange that Buddhism is so little approached in Demon. The God Machine has several attributes of Mara.</div> </div> </div> </div>SMT Mara? NSFW <a href=\"https://megamitensei.fandom.com/wiki/Mara\" target=\"_blank\">https://megamitensei.fandom.com/wiki/Mara</a><br /> <br /> Cause that\u2019s hilarious. I\u2019m just imagine a Angel who\u2019s true From is a giant dick demon.<br /> <br /> But I think you mean M\u0101ra as Skandha-m\u0101ra, or M\u0101ra as metaphor for the entirety of conditioned existence.<br /> <br /> A Demiurge Like figure .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23952,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","user":"Konradleijon","date":". 04-02-2019, 06:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T15:38:36-07:00","id":1302029,"title":"","content":"So,i've been in a host mood lately. and i wanted to discuss,what do you guys think is the hosts's role in the contagion,would them try to help the contagion spread?maybe join the Naglfar's army?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T16:08:35-07:00","id":1302035,"title":"","content":"It's easy to see them joining any of the False. But you could have arguments for them joining up with Zero Hour (if Contagion threatens their progenitor reconstitution), or the Theseans (perhaps they can use Contagion to skip some steps), or the Rosetta Society (which may help them find hidden shards or other vestiges that can guide their drive)..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T16:21:38-07:00","id":1302038,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1302035#post1302035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's easy to see them joining any of the False. But you could have arguments for them joining up with Zero Hour (if Contagion threatens their progenitor reconstitution), or the Theseans (perhaps they can use Contagion to skip some steps), or the Rosetta Society (which may help them find hidden shards or other vestiges that can guide their drive)..</div> </div> </div> </div>That's very well thought! Something else i considered was that the average host could evolve with the help of the Sworn or False,with Vectirs they could rise above their animalistic instincts, or guide them to more constructive goals. i can even picture some Edges Hosts might have","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T16:38:23-07:00","id":1302043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1301980#post1301980\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Beast Edge for Drain Energy in the Contagion Vector might want to be looked at. Having your Satiety skyrocket to 10 isn't as good of a thing for Beasts as refilling Aether for Demons or Glamour for Changeling is.<br /> <br /> As it is, I'm not sure why a False Beast would want to slap themselves with the Slumbering Condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is intended to give the Beast Satiety so that they can Expend it on their Atavisms and Lair traits more readily, without being to worries about Starving","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T16:53:51-07:00","id":1302053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1302043#post1302043\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it is intended to give the Beast Satiety so that they can Expend it on their Atavisms and Lair traits more readily, without being to worries about Starving</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I get what the intent is. It's to replenish resources for spenditures, as you say. But Beasts have Satiety Conditions that adjust based on what value the Beast is currently at with their Satiety. And when a Beast hits Satiety 10, they get the Slumbering Condition immediately. This means that the Beast loses access to all of their Atavisms and Nightmares. The Beast is also explicitly restricted from spending Satiety for any reason.<br /> <br /> So, it's very bad news for a Beast. Especially for a Beast that would associate with the False.<br /> <br /> I don't think this power is meant to be something that screws over the wielder as hard as it does for Beasts.<br /> <br /> Edit: Basically, it looks like the writer just knew that Beasts spend Satiety as their resource and went &quot;Well, they get fill up with that then!&quot; without knowing what that actually means for the mechanics of the game. And okay, it's hard to know all the details about all the different gamelines. But <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar152_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"152\" data-vbnamecard=\"152\">The Gentleman Gamer</a> might want to double-check this as to whether it's appropriate as this is a great time to do corrections if they feel something needs to be adjusted, which I think is in their discretion.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":851,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","user":"Paradim","date":". 04-02-2019, 08:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T17:08:21-07:00","id":1302056,"title":"","content":"....just remember to hold onto any oddities you find in the text when the errata phase does come, folks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T17:13:17-07:00","id":1302058,"title":"","content":"Do Vampires and Sin-Eaters count as &quot;living things&quot; for the purpose of deciding who gets damaged by Drain Energy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T17:41:12-07:00","id":1302064,"title":"","content":"Contagion *, Purge Weakness, &quot;System: A member of the False who inflicts one point of <i><b>unsoakable </b></i>lethal damage on herself can ignore the effects of a specific supernatural weakness..&quot;<br /> <br /> Soaking damage is oWOD. I assume the intent is <i>Resistant</i> damage.<br /> <br /> Also, the Werewolf Edge, &quot;Werewolves: The touch of silver no longer causes pain to a werewolf for the duration of a scene...&quot;<br /> <br /> The touch of silver only causes discomfort to the Pure. The Forsaken only suffer aggravated damage from silver weapons.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T17:54:51-07:00","id":1302066,"title":"","content":"Authority Vector ***, Plutomancy<br /> &quot;Money. They say it makes the world go \u2018round. They probably don\u2019t mean it literally. But for your bureau, it\u2019s true. Maybe it\u2019s something you picked up from the study of financial contagion, and thinking how those economic strategies map to the Contagion you\u2019re fighting now. Maybe all that time you spent around mages has rubbed off on you, imparting a little bit of that <i><b>'coincidental magic'</b></i> they keep talking about.&quot;<br /> <br /> No coincidental/vulgar magic in Mage 2e.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T18:40:51-07:00","id":1302077,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1302064#post1302064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Soaking damage is oWOD. I assume the intent is <i>Resistant</i> damage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fairly certain the intent is just damage that can't be blocked by armor. Matthew is aware of the WoD terminology that's leaked in, though, and mentioned it a few pages back as something that will be fixed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>branford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1302066#post1302066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No coincidental/vulgar magic in Mage 2e.</div> </div> </div> </div>Bit worse than that, coincidental is also a WoD term. The term in 1E Awakening was 'covert'.<br /> <br /> It's possible that this is meant to describe the 'coincidental' effects of Long-Term Nimbus, but that seems unlikely given the frequency that we've been seeing WoD terminology in this and other recent OPP drafts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3570,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","user":"lnodiv","date":". 04-02-2019, 10:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T18:57:22-07:00","id":1302080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1302053#post1302053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I get what the intent is. It's to replenish resources for spenditures, as you say. But Beasts have Satiety Conditions that adjust based on what value the Beast is currently at with their Satiety. And when a Beast hits Satiety 10, they get the Slumbering Condition immediately. This means that the Beast loses access to all of their Atavisms and Nightmares. The Beast is also explicitly restricted from spending Satiety for any reason.<br /> <br /> So, it's very bad news for a Beast. Especially for a Beast that would associate with the False.<br /> <br /> I don't think this power is meant to be something that screws over the wielder as hard as it does for Beasts.<br /> <br /> Edit: Basically, it looks like the writer just knew that Beasts spend Satiety as their resource and went &amp;quot;Well, they get fill up with that then!&amp;quot; without knowing what that actually means for the mechanics of the game. And okay, it's hard to know all the details about all the different gamelines. But <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> might want to double-check this as to whether it's appropriate as this is a great time to do corrections if they feel something needs to be adjusted, which I think is in their discretion.</div> </div> </div> </div>That does appear to be a genuine oversight, yeah, probably due to time constraints and a lapse in proof reading.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, this Vector does deal with the Contagion, so perhaps is was intentionally done this way, to show that one CAN get screwed over royally.<br /> <br /> But.. I\u2019m not really sure this is a particularly bad thing. Then again, I am biased against Beasts, so take that with a handful of Salt!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T19:00:45-07:00","id":1302082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1302077#post1302077\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Matt is aware of the WoD terminology that's leaked in, though, and mentioned it a few pages back as something that will be fixed.</div> </div> </div> </div>FYI, his preferred name is Matthew, not Matt. <br /> <br /> (I point this out because someone else pointed it out to me once upon a time)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T19:02:45-07:00","id":1302083,"title":"","content":"It's a little disconcerting that a late draft of a CofD crossover book seems to include a lot oWOD references. CofD crossover dealing with different editions and unreleased products has enough potential issues without concerns about confusion without a totally separate gameline and setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/618-branford","name":"branford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar618_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1904"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T19:04:03-07:00","id":1302084,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1302082#post1302082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(I point this out because someone else pointed it out to me once upon a time)</div> </div> </div> </div>Fixed, thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T19:09:42-07:00","id":1302085,"title":"","content":"What level of the Poisoned tilt should be caused by the Crucible Initiative Specialization for Drain Energy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12738-minty","name":"Minty","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T19:10:15-07:00","id":1302086,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1302080#post1302080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That does appear to be a genuine oversight, yeah, probably due to time constraints and a lapse in proof reading.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, this Vector does deal with the Contagion, so perhaps is was intentionally done this way, to show that one CAN get screwed over royally.<br /> <br /> But.. I\u2019m not really sure this is a particularly bad thing. Then again, I am biased against Beasts, so take that with a handful of Salt!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd be willing to wager money that it wasn't intentionally done this way. Any effort to show that the Contagion Vector can screw someone over will not be restricted to just negatively impacting Beasts for a single power. If that was the intention, they'd open all the supernatural types to that (and kind of did, I think, by having you get infected by the Contagion).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T19:19:38-07:00","id":1302088,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1302080#post1302080\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But.. I\u2019m not really sure this is a particularly bad thing. Then again, I am biased against Beasts, so take that with a handful of Salt!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I mean, I know if I wanted to demonstrate how dangerous the Contagion could be, it would be something that affected only a single splat, in a single power, in a way that reads like a very obvious oversight and not an intentional demonstration at all.<br /> <br /> It's <i>obviously</i> not intended. The danger in the Contagion here is expressed by the effect on the environment, the fuel replenishment is the benefit gained for that price - the fact that Beasts aren't affected the same way is an obvious oversight based on the fact that their fuel stat works entirely differently from the rest, and not an intentional effort to screw them over in particular.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3570-lnodiv","name":"lnodiv","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3570_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1607"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T19:28:58-07:00","id":1302091,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1302011#post1302011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, also the Godhead Vector costs way too much, and has a wonky Duration; it's one Willpower or two lethal damage per turn to maintain, when a lot of its powers cost Willpower and assuming it costs three, and it's said to last a scene when it can explicitly lapse if keeping it up gets too tiring.</div> </div> </div> </div> The Godhood power also has an issue for Vampires with blood potency 10 already. Could it be possible a Vampire to end up with BP 12 and what would that look like?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T20:13:58-07:00","id":1302101,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>lnodiv</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1302088#post1302088\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I mean, I know if I wanted to demonstrate how dangerous the Contagion could be, it would be something that affected only a single splat, in a single power, in a way that reads like a very obvious oversight and not an intentional demonstration at all.<br /> <br /> It's <i>obviously</i> not intended. The danger in the Contagion here is expressed by the effect on the environment, the fuel replenishment is the benefit gained for that price - the fact that Beasts aren't affected the same way is an obvious oversight based on the fact that their fuel stat works entirely differently from the rest, and not an intentional effort to screw them over in particular.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank God(Machine) you don\u2019t write for them then, You\u2019d be a loose cannon madman!<br /> <br /> And I know, it was something I thought about when talking to a friend who likes Beast a little too much and was making a big deal out of it, and thought it would be a dickish, though funny mechanical Quirk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1686,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","user":"Korogra","date":". 04-02-2019, 11:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T20:26:02-07:00","id":1302102,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1302086#post1302086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd be willing to wager money that it wasn't intentionally done this way. Any effort to show that the Contagion Vector can screw someone over will not be restricted to just negatively impacting Beasts for a single power. If that was the intention, they'd open all the supernatural types to that (and kind of did, I think, by having you get infected by the Contagion).</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019d be willing to wager that it wasn\u2019t either, because that means free money for the both of us.<br /> <br /> But now that I think about it, individual penalties/side effect specific to each splat for using contagion vectors sounds pretty fun, I might do that in my game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T20:39:40-07:00","id":1302104,"title":"","content":"Oh god, I just realized I have to go back to Discord someday.<br /> <br /> There are Princess Edges to write! And justifications as to why any of them would go False. Which I can find easily (even for ones that aren't the Crucible Initiative), but still. Reason to finally come out of hibernation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T20:48:52-07:00","id":1302105,"title":"","content":"I love the vectors, a lot of fun, but a few thoughts. <br /> <br /> Evolve can lead to some seriously weird out comes. Like a Hunter Embracing someone as a Vampire, or making them their Ghoul. A Changeling casting powerful blood sorcery magic like creating a Blood God using their Glamour pool, or making Tass out of their Glamour pool. Glamour is WAY more plentiful and accessible then any other magical resource, a mage could end up with a huge mana/tass stockpile that way. A Sin Eater could lend out its ability to come back from dying to say Deviant. A magic would lend its ability to summon supernall entities to a Vampire, which I figure would be very confusing to it. It just gets weirder from there.<br /> <br /> Contagion vector would be super tempting for Ordo Dracul Vampires especially, no more worrying about Sunlight, the ability to shift away contagion, feed upon the enviroment itself, and more. Its the kind of liberty from the Vampire weaknesses they dream of.<br /> <br /> Also a True Fae False is scary, no vulneriblity to iron.<br /> <br /> Hobgoblins would also love it, as of all fae they have the hardest time gaining Glamour, just drain it out of their enviroment. <br /> <br /> I think alot of creatures are going to be attracted to the False not just out of fear of the Contagion, but because alot of the powers seemed to protect them from the weaknesses and suffering of their own template. <br /> <br /> I think a Changeling will be particularly attracted to the powers of the Jeremaid, the low level powers help with clarity/sanity, which can be problem for Changelings and those around them. And the higher level powers give them unique magics to fight the True Fae with, ones immune to iron.<br /> <br /> Also any none intergrator demon that sees Godhead abused to the point that the user gets absorbed by the Godmachine is going to concider the Jeremiad a dangerous enemy and servant of the Godmachine (which it kind of is, in a very weird way).<br /> <br /> Also Modern Miracle is unclear in it's abilities and limitations of what it can do. Like could it raise all allies in the area from the dead like a mass resurrect spell, while just automatically killing all none infected enemies? And the cost is too high, it's powerful I think, but not only do you use it only once, period, bit it cost a Willpower Dot AND a Sworn XP. <br /> <br /> Godhead is interesting, but it should be make clear that the self inflicted damage heals like normal wounds do on mortals, it's just immune to magical healing. Otherwise it sounds like permenant damage.<br /> <br /> And is it intended that you aren't just immune to wound penalties, but actual new damage (excluding the damage Godhead itself deals to you) as well. Like if while using Godhead someone one shots you at point blank range, it deals no health damage? <br /> <br /> Also two things are mentioned, but not explained, Sophia and Agora (I assume Sophia is just the characters religion/philosophy, I could be wrong). <br /> <br /> Also I could see Seekers of the Throne and Circle of the Crone as being just as attracted to the Jeremaid as Lanca Santum, they have their own religious beliefs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T22:44:19-07:00","id":1302117,"title":"","content":"Evolve is wonderful, isn\u2019t it?<br /> <br /> And the False offers opportunities for so many monsters to jump in on the Fun, I personally plan to bring several recurring antagonists from my games together as members of Naglfar\u2019s Army and the Crucible Initiative!<br /> <br /> As for Agora, that is the term for a group of Theseans working together.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T22:49:07-07:00","id":1302118,"title":"","content":"Well Plague Angel-Possessed Sin-Eaters and Werewolves are terrifying.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T22:56:21-07:00","id":1302119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1302118#post1302118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well Plague Angel-Possessed Sin-Eaters and Werewolves are terrifying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don\u2019t threaten us with a good time, Kell","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T23:06:48-07:00","id":1302122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1302105#post1302105\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also two things are mentioned, but not explained, Sophia and Agora (I assume Sophia is just the characters religion/philosophy, I could be wrong)..</div> </div> </div> </div>I think Sophia was already talked about already as some sort of focus going to assume from requirements its probably anything you want just has to be something your character can focus on<br /> <br /> Requirement: Access to a representation of the fanatic\u2019s sophia \u2014 a bible, a sacred fire, a spirit, whatever.<br /> <br /> As for agora its described as public open space or used for assemblies or market... going to guess its just a term for a teamwork pool","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/893-reaperfrost8","name":"reaperfrost8","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar893_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-02T23:53:00-07:00","id":1302131,"title":"","content":"(reads the Drained Tilt) ...so this is the deep backstory of Dark Sun. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Any plans for Edges suitable to normally antagonistic types who go Sworn?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25206-evil-midnight-lurker","name":"Evil Midnight Lurker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25206_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T00:53:39-07:00","id":1302137,"title":"","content":"Reading through Vectors again I noticed beasts have an issue with the Evolve power as well. It states you can either use your own resource pool or the character you borrowed the powers froms one but for a beast Satiety is vastly more important than say Vitae. <br /> <br /> Any other splat borrowing from a beast gets a huge advantage as unlocking the Satiety-Expenditure bonus for the trivial cost of one Vitae is a no-brainer whereas beasts are looking at spending half their Satiety to use the most basic powers. <br /> <br /> Might be worth adding that Satiety is worth &quot;X&quot; amount of other resources to balance it out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25080-kargle18446","name":"Kargle18446","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T02:56:49-07:00","id":1302148,"title":"","content":"This is useful feedback, thank you!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T03:38:51-07:00","id":1302153,"title":"","content":"I wrote the Drain Energy power - the Beast version accidentally screwing them via high Satiety associated effects was an oversight on my part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T04:29:40-07:00","id":1302160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1302153#post1302153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wrote the Drain Energy power - the Beast version accidentally screwing them via high Satiety associated effects was an oversight on my part.</div> </div> </div> </div> It's still a cool power in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T04:36:46-07:00","id":1302162,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Gentleman Gamer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1302148#post1302148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is useful feedback, thank you!</div> </div> </div> </div> Your welcome","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T05:00:58-07:00","id":1302166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1302118#post1302118\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well Plague Angel-Possessed Sin-Eaters and Werewolves are terrifying.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait where?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23952-konradleijon","name":"Konradleijon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23952_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1441"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T06:45:35-07:00","id":1302187,"title":"","content":"Guys, I have homebrewed some Host Edges.<br /> <br /> check it out!<br /> Host Edges for the Fervor Vector<br /> <br /> \u2022 Purification<br /> Hosts are disrupting force through and through,they are about building power by absorbing themselve into an<br /> terrible amalgamation. with this Edge,they can waive the Willpower cost of purification,instead they sacrifice another<br /> Host to their progenitor torning his enemy apart to shed the Condition.<br /> \u2022\u2022 Divine Revelation<br /> Ironically,many of the more lucid Hosts place value in loyalty. After all,when you are a god-fragment trying to recuparate your<br /> former glory,it pays to have loyal helpers. By spending one more Willpower point,the Host can inflict the Mesmerized condition<br /> on the target of this Vector,as well as the normal effect of the power.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Cleansing Flame<br /> The Hosts,remember what they once were. Not in their minds,but in their flesh and bone. When they reach for the Heavens<br /> to wield the Sacred fire,they are indeed calling on the remains of their Progenitor. With Cleansing Flame<br /> they can infect the victims of this power with a Shard of themselves.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Modern Miracle<br /> Hosts are in many ways,profanity given shape. They corrupt the Gauntlet,the sacred barrier between the Flesh and Shadow.<br /> therefore they can choose to affect targets on both sides of the Gauntlet with their Miracles.<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Godhead<br /> Make no mistake,Hosts were once Gods,they were monsters and scavengers and plagues,but above all else,they were Gods.<br /> And now,it's time for them to reclaim their ancient glory and birthright.<br /> When they use godhead,they can affect te Gauntlet without any Essence cost,and they can choose to harm the Gauntlet in one turn<br /> as if they were harming it for a month.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T06:47:02-07:00","id":1302188,"title":"","content":"I noticed some issues with the godhead vector. Like certain edges if borrowed makes the others obsolete: the Demon going loud one for example makes the vampire edge obsolete. As going loud effectively raises the supernatural potency trait of demons(Primium) to 10, so if you borrow that edge then the vampire edge does not really do anything. Secondly if you are a hunter and borrow edges from this one, some of them might not even do anything as there is no potency trait for you to raise or any vitae or spells for you hold/keep up","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions"