t1302397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fair. NEW TOPIC.<br /> <br /> Actually, old one, favorite Vectors? I'll admit, I'm kind of sucker for Fire For Effect. It just kind of begs for one of those &amp;quot;Stride in and win&amp;quot; scenes even if it's not neccesarily as powerful as plenty of it's peers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love Godhead! Not only because I like big showy spectacles,but because it makes each of the splat members to become one with their respective progenitor.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T18:41:37-07:00","id":1302405,"title":"","content":"I'm a little Torn between Semiontics and Intel. Heck, the latter has me reconsidering Zero Hour and it's philosophy entirely in light of how one leads to the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T18:47:36-07:00","id":1302411,"title":"","content":"On terms of over all favorite, Realignment tickles a lot of my fancies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T19:01:05-07:00","id":1302415,"title":"","content":"I like Realignment, Intel and Fervor the most...i am so and so about authority and feel rather underwhelmed by at least the latter stages of Semiotics","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T20:35:53-07:00","id":1302433,"title":"","content":"So, I've got a bit of a hang up with some of the Vectors. I'm not really sure how some of them translate into something achievable through growth, development or investment. Authority, I get. It has a lot of flavor text describing occult paradigms mixed with technology for providing access or through similar ideas with social engineering. Fervor, I also get. Since Fervor is basically the power of faith and such. But I really struggle with, say... Intel. How does that get developed? It seems kind of like psychic powers?<br /> <br /> I dunno, I really feel like I'm missing something here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/851-paradim","name":"Paradim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar851_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T20:48:38-07:00","id":1302436,"title":"","content":"An analyst integrator with Godhead is about the strongest a character can get, at least easily, and I love the concepts involved as well, so that's my go to for a stronk, positive character from now on. It seems to be the holy grail of the integrator ideal as well.<br /> <br /> A False Beast with Control Contagion, on the other hand, is what I've been wanting for a long time, a way for a beast kinship to interface with angels and demons. I have a couple beasts holding out for that, ones created through chambers created by the unchained, and my wife's beast char is likely to seek that as well, just to start establishing kinship with GM creatures.<br /> <br /> I can't wait to find out how stronk the Contagious can be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-03T21:08:56-07:00","id":1302441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Paradim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1302433#post1302433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I've got a bit of a hang up with some of the Vectors. I'm not really sure how some of them translate into something achievable through growth, development or investment. Authority, I get. It has a lot of flavor text describing occult paradigms mixed with technology for providing access or through similar ideas with social engineering. Fervor, I also get. Since Fervor is basically the power of faith and such. But I really struggle with, say... Intel. How does that get developed? It seems kind of like psychic powers?<br /> <br /> I dunno, I really feel like I'm missing something here.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Seems to me like it's a natural extension of Zero Company's aesthetic of intelligent discipline over raw strength and rage; after learning the basics of how to both spot enemies and alert your unit, you gradually merge your wills into a gestalt instinct that is greater than the sum of its parts. Given how Vectors are explicitly supernatural, that appears as psychic powers, but it's not at all different from what basic training is supposed to do - in a war, you need to be able to read your buddies' actions by instinct to coordinate at peak efficiency, which means higher chance of survival. You'll notice that they have the earliest dot rating where they start needing Teamwork actions, because their method of war requires comrades.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"d