get=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T14:06:06-07:00","id":1399370,"title":"","content":"Backer PDF is getting sent out to everyone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-27T14:18:52-07:00","id":1399378,"title":"","content":"Got it, and I will note as I have elsewhere that there are more Specializations in the Vectors, so that's neat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-08T16:10:54-07:00","id":1401798,"title":"","content":"So, no one's mentioned it, so I will.<br /> <br /> Why does the Beast Edge for Drain Energy from the Contagion Vector now offer three dice for imposing Lair Traits instead of just....raising Satiety to 9?<br /> <br /> Like, the Satiety 10 thing was an error, but all it needed was a single number change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-09T13:51:04-07:00","id":1401959,"title":"","content":"More intriguing: Is there any difference between the Elodoth specialty of Comprehension (Semiotics 1) and the passive benefit of the power available to everyone?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1937-treelior","name":"Treelior","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-16T08:33:59-07:00","id":1403102,"title":"","content":"My disappointment with the new version of the pdf is immeasurable. Godhead and Purge Weakness, in particular, have been ruined. Fervor has always been a weak, poorly designed Vector, with the only powers in the game that cost experience to use, but with Godhead being a once per chronicle thing, Fervor has like one<br /> <br /> Likewise, Purge Weakness is a weaker version of Renewal, for example, blocking sunlight only instead of fire and sunlight, and now it permanently wrecks your character as the &quot;advantage&quot; for the Machiavellian Gambit, and screws you up long-term otherwise.<br /> <br /> Since I'm mostly into crossover, the new version is so bad that its rather lessened my enthusiasm for CofD in general.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-16T10:59:46-07:00","id":1403118,"title":"","content":"Do you think there is any hope for a vector renewal?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-16T13:27:47-07:00","id":1403148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Deinos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1403102#post1403102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My disappointment with the new version of the pdf is immeasurable. Godhead and Purge Weakness, in particular, have been ruined. Fervor has always been a weak, poorly designed Vector, with the only powers in the game that cost experience to use, but with Godhead being a once per chronicle thing, Fervor has like one<br /> <br /> Likewise, Purge Weakness is a weaker version of Renewal, for example, blocking sunlight only instead of fire and sunlight, and now it permanently wrecks your character as the &quot;advantage&quot; for the Machiavellian Gambit, and screws you up long-term otherwise.<br /> <br /> Since I'm mostly into crossover, the new version is so bad that its rather lessened my enthusiasm for CofD in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have checked both my Kickstarter copy and the PDF and I have to seriously ask what the hell you are on about-I cannot find these details in either copy.<br /> <br /> EDIT: okay, I found the Renewal part where it corresponds for vampires, and for everyone who has that Edge, yeah, Renewal is the better deal, I apologize for missing that.<br /> <br /> EDIT: And found the Godhead thing as well, so nvm, you're good.<br /> <br /> That aside, I'm not sure I agree with the disappointment, but I get where it's coming from.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-16-2020, 05:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T13:49:52-07:00","id":1414961,"title":"","content":"*checks email*<br /> <br /> Oh hey, the Finalized PDF for the book is now up for Backers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-21T20:23:21-07:00","id":1415012,"title":"","content":"...and it's going to be out for everyone this Wednesday!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T00:00:53-07:00","id":1415024,"title":"","content":"Why did they even make Fervor cost permanent XP? Whose idea was this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11876-deinos","name":"Deinos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"311"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T03:11:18-07:00","id":1415037,"title":"","content":"My disappointment isn't immeasurable, but it does suck seeing what was announced as a crossover focused book turn into what's mostly a game-agnostic* campaign book. On top of that, the things that are included to facilitate crossover play (i.e. Sworn/False &amp; Vectors) is really clunky and generally disappointing and not something I would want to use in my games.<br /> <br /> In fact, the moment I stop thinking about it as a crossover book it becomes much better:<br /> The main part of the book (i.e. the Contagion and example settings) ranges from decent to really interesting. I like how the Contagion is described and the guide for designing your own strains. Example settings is something I'm rarely interested in, but I think they might be great for those who are. In fact, I really liked the Antarctican setting so much that I might use it almost as is rather than just as inspiration, which is rare for me.<br /> My only real complaint on the book after the first chapter (which, for all I care, could be completely excised) is the pervasive focus on the God-Machine. It's patient zero in almost all examples, and the singular exception still heavily hints towards it. That makes the book less useful (but far from completely useless) for those who might not want to use the God-Machine in their games. It also plays directly into the (otherwise mistaken) perception that CofD is overly focused on the God-Machine which turned away some people when GMC came out. Hopefully that notion has mostly been dispelled at this point.<br /> <br /> *by game-agnostic I mean something that fit each of the different gamelines, but not necessarily crossover games","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T06:10:53-07:00","id":1415054,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I agree with that sentiment. IIRC, the Player's Guide was said to have more focus about Crossover than the CC itself, but I still felt that the Contagion was so big that there wasn't much room to explore how the different gamelines actually interact through a crossover, both mechanically and setting wise. Dark Eras (especially DE2) have actually gave much more material to work with in terms of gameline-gamelines interactions than the CC- but again, hopefully the Player's Guide will give some of the tools to deal with it.<br /> <br /> I also wonder how my pitches for the Contagion Outbreaks would end up. I assume we will see them in Global Outbreaks, so it would take some time, but I do wonder to which directions they took it. Well, I'll just have to wait and see.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T07:21:58-07:00","id":1415065,"title":"","content":"I was honestly disappointed most that the GM was basically the source of it all. I mean I love the God machine, but I wanted the Contagion to very mysterious, not just a glorified glitch in the matrix.<br /> <br /> And yeah, the crossover is not really at the forefront. Kinda odd","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T08:34:28-07:00","id":1415072,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1415065#post1415065\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was honestly disappointed most that the GM was basically the source of it all. I mean I love the God machine, but I wanted the Contagion to very mysterious, not just a glorified glitch in the matrix.<br /> <br /> And yeah, the crossover is not really at the forefront. Kinda odd</div> </div> </div> </div>VECTOR. THe GM is a primary VECTOR for Contagion. It is NOT the SOURCE.<br /> <br /> We Have Done This Song and Dance Too Many Times To Keep Saying It.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T08:44:43-07:00","id":1415074,"title":"","content":"An understandable misconception considering the heavy focus on the God-Machine as the primary vector.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T09:07:35-07:00","id":1415076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1415074#post1415074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An understandable misconception considering the heavy focus on the God-Machine as the primary vector.</div> </div> </div> </div>Presuming the notion I ignore that reading the book past the admittedly deceptive opening of the book and thus see clearly from the rest of the book that the Contagion is possibly sourced from multiple origins and that cross-contamination allows for further mutation and that the God-Machine is so prevalent because it is a worldwide entity of physical and ephemeral nature that both internally and externally shuffles elements around, thus making it unlikely to that it's<i> not</i> somehow involved in the spreading of weird reality diseases-<br /> <br /> Presuming I give the benefit of the doubt to a new reader,...this conversation has <i>still</i> been had with everyone in the room. I am very clearly <i>not</i> talking to new readers. At this point it reads less as miscomprehension and more like willfully sticking to your guns rather than adjust your arguments.<br /> <br /> I get how the opening creates an impression, and I can even agree that's something that probably could be done better, but this argument is not that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T10:31:55-07:00","id":1415081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1415072#post1415072\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">VECTOR. THe GM is a primary VECTOR for Contagion. It is NOT the SOURCE.<br /> <br /> We Have Done This Song and Dance Too Many Times To Keep Saying It.</div> </div> </div> </div>My bad. It's just featured so many times I made the faulty assumption","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T10:37:44-07:00","id":1415085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Primordial newcomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1415081#post1415081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My bad. It's just featured so many times I made the faulty assumption</div> </div> </div> </div>S'all good. It's just annoying to come across a new misconception with memetic strength when it seems like we finally got other ones like Changelings Inevtiably Become True Fae and Second Edition Is All About the God-Machine put to bed in the communtiy.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T11:58:40-07:00","id":1415099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1415085#post1415085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">S'all good. It's just annoying to come across a new misconception with memetic strength when it seems like we finally got other ones like Changelings Inevtiably Become True Fae and Second Edition Is All About the God-Machine put to bed in the communtiy.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah I understand lol. And I hate to have contributed to that line of thinking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T21:17:33-07:00","id":1415163,"title":"","content":"It is based in the book itself, where the only shown origin of Contagion ARE related to God Machine... I do not remember 'here are other ideas from where Contagion can come' frame in the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-22T21:41:41-07:00","id":1415165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1415163#post1415163\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is based in the book itself, where the only shown origin of Contagion ARE related to God Machine... I do not remember 'here are other ideas from where Contagion can come' frame in the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>The one in the setting most relevant to Demon has its cause tied to a temporal clusterfuck whose roots include a thing from the Abyss and a thing from the Underworld; the God-Machine's role in the mess in Sittard is almost solely that of exacerbated autoimmune disorder. I think the site most relevant to the gameline where the God-Machine is the biggest deal not having its Contagion originate from the Machine is about as damning an indictment of the misconception as can be made without dedicating pagespace specifically to assuaging fears on the same attentive wavelength as half the memetic bad press Beast still gets.<br /> <br /> The God-Machine's an ascendant structural parasite on the world that may or may not be a former piece of the thing that makes the world make sense. Contagion is bits of the world going haywire in a transmissible fashion. You can't really have a crossover setup that doesn't engage with that without cutting Demon out of the picture and/or trading off to the older antifandom misconception of &quot;Mages did everything&quot; or similar.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-09-23T11:19:20-07:00","id":1415213,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/318347/Chronicles-of-Darkness-The-Contagion-Chronicle?affiliate_id=498510\" target=\"_blank\">And it is out to the public! </a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T12:21:52-07:00","id":1453959,"title":"","content":"PG for the Contagion Chronicle Backer PDF is now available to backers!<br /> <br /> EDIT: Errata Google Form link here: <a href=\"https://forms.gle/94tJFieVC11cdJzh7\" target=\"_blank\">https://forms.gle/94tJFieVC11cdJzh7</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 07-01-2021, 03:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T13:52:28-07:00","id":1453963,"title":"","content":"Re: Player's Guide<br /> <br /> I'm disappointed that Promethean stuff is Fate (+Life/Death) based, since it just doesn't make sense to me, and wish it were Matter + Death or Matter + Prime. I also wish there was more info on how Prime interacts with non-Awakened &quot;magic&quot; and what, specifically, <i>counts</i> as &quot;magic&quot; since Blood Sorcery seems not to.<br /> <br /> Otherwise I rather like the information presented, the various crossover information is nice to have, and I like the shared Merits presented.<br /> <br /> For a 30-page stretch supplement it's pretty jam-packed with info, and I like it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1452235-proin-s-legacy-hub\" target=\"_blank\">proin's Legacy hub</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2757-proindrakenzol","name":"proindrakenzol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1514"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T14:26:41-07:00","id":1453966,"title":"","content":"Personally, I think the Promethean crossover stuff should have referenced Prime rather than Fate; and that's how I'm going to rule it in my games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T15:35:56-07:00","id":1453986,"title":"","content":"I agree on the promethean front I think prime is better than fate to explain them divine fire. Beyond that I noticed one little line that I like but that I think needs more context..the thing about others being able to learn blood sorcery. There are two things I would want to see be adressed: 1. How do non Vampires use Cruac specifically since it is powered through Vitae. 2. How do Theban Sorcery and Cruac impact the morality meters of the other splats if they got them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-01T15:45:18-07:00","id":1453990,"title":"","content":"Non-vampires use Cruac through sacrifice; this is addressed in <b>Blood Sorcery</b>, under the Sons of Phobos.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-02T01:58:03-07:00","id":1454056,"title":"","content":"the only thing I wished that this book would have adressed are non-affiliated minor templates like The Plain, Lost Boys, and similar joining the Sworn or the False and how Vectors work for them. And I would have liked maybe a couple of more outlets for how to spend Faction XP or whatever they call it(was it Sworn Beats)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-02T03:28:29-07:00","id":1454062,"title":"","content":"Pyros is the stuff of change and transformation. Metaphorical change in the Arcana is a function of Time (the momentum) and Fate (the direction) - qashmallim are literally manifestations of the force of universal change that emerge with a direction (their Principle) in mind.<br /> <br /> Prime, conversely, is ummutable, fixed Truth. Why on earth would affecting Pyros' creations require Prime?<br /> <br /> I mean, I *get* why. It's because of the surface trappings, Prime's pairing with Forces and the fact that Prometheans see Pyros as a flame, etc. But it's on the level of getting hung up on Arcadia being called the same thing in English as Arcadia, and not realising the Hedge and C!Arcadia resemble Pandemonium waaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaay more than they resemble real Arcadia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000000\"><b>Dave Brookshaw</b></span>","edited":{"userid":14,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","user":"Dave Brookshaw","date":". 07-02-2021, 06:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/14-dave-brookshaw","name":"Dave Brookshaw","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar14_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2081"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-02T03:44:55-07:00","id":1454064,"title":"","content":"Fate magic seems to get the lion\u2019s share of interacting with the \u2018Fallen supernatural\u2019 stuff, from the Forge Destiny spell to Faerie stuff, God-Machine\u2019s angel stuff, some parts of the Mummy\u2019s Fate stuff (but mostly Ren), and now Pyretic stuff.<br /> <br /> And though I don\u2019t have the aforementioned Player\u2019s Guide yet and thus have no clue, I like to imagine Dhampirs, knowledge of the more esoteric effects of spiritual Resonance that werewolves take granted for, the Keys of death embedded in Mementos, and Beastly Legend-building and Heroic Anathema are all at least tangentially related to the Fate Arcanum.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Now Vitriol, otoh, feels like it should be primarily Death Arcanum stuff\u2026 can anybody confirm or deny this, please?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":12619,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","user":"21C Hermit","date":". 07-02-2021, 09:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-02T08:01:51-07:00","id":1454079,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1454064#post1454064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Now Vitriol, otoh, feels like it should be primarily Death Arcanum stuff\u2026 can anybody confirm or deny this, please?</div> </div> </div> </div>Vitriol registers to Life, Matter, and Fate, with Death and Matter being alluded to in that Vitriol is the physical manifestation of the Pilgrimage's progress.<br /> <br /> Which primarily makes sense-vitriol is the substance that interacts with the Divine Fire and the Promethean's body to bind together into the making of a real boy.<br /> <br /> Fate getting the lion's share of function stems from the fact that a lot of the big tier entities relying on what amounts to &quot;chaos magic&quot; emanating from their presence, with lower key entities often being the trailing off of those effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-02T10:50:22-07:00","id":1454090,"title":"","content":"I'm gonna pop in and say that I personally thought Fate makes a lot of sense for stuff related to the Divine Fire, for the reasons previously stated, but also especially how the section starts with the Pilgrimage, setting the stage for everything else. I mean, it is possibly the most defining aspect of the Divine Fire, especially as it relates to the Created. Even without the section spelling it out, it is easy to interpret it as a destiny [or Destiny] for every Promethean, one they receive prophetic dreams about. That is pretty Fate-y. Plus, every <i><i>qashmal</i></i> is an agent of a specific future or event; hard to be Fate-ier than that. Hell, the way Disquiet affects behavior can even be interpreted through Fate, which is really, really <i>weird</i> and fun. I kind of love it.<br /> <br /> And obviously, this is all a gross over-simplification, because it always is [and should be] more complicated than a single Arcanum. And the fact that practically every aspect of the Promethean condition requires a totally different conjunctional Arcana illustrates as much.<br /> <br /> Personally, I was more intrigued that manipulating blood bonds is Space, and that a blood bond's effects appear to follow the sympathetic link. It is kind of obvious in retrospect, but has some <i>really</i> interesting implications to me, at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Posting gives me anxiety, but I'm still happy to be here</i><br /> Habitual Lurker, Vengrel Liker, Acolyte Apologist, She/Her","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25955-somethingfishy","name":"SomethingFishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25955_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-02T15:15:12-07:00","id":1454099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1454064#post1454064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fate magic seems to get the lion\u2019s share of interacting with the \u2018Fallen supernatural\u2019 stuff, from the Forge Destiny spell to Faerie stuff, God-Machine\u2019s angel stuff, some parts of the Mummy\u2019s Fate stuff (but mostly Ren), and now Pyretic stuff.<br /> <br /> And though I don\u2019t have the aforementioned Player\u2019s Guide yet and thus have no clue, I like to imagine Dhampirs, knowledge of the more esoteric effects of spiritual Resonance that werewolves take granted for, the Keys of death embedded in Mementos, and Beastly Legend-building and Heroic Anathema are all at least tangentially related to the Fate Arcanum.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Now Vitriol, otoh, feels like it should be primarily Death Arcanum stuff\u2026 can anybody confirm or deny this, please?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, they put spiritual Resonance under Prime (as an example of natural law), though anything can mess with it via the common sense rule; if the Resonance is calm, quiet stillness then Forces can mess that up the same way a rave can.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-02T15:17:43-07:00","id":1454100,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1454099#post1454099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, they put spiritual Resonance under Prime (as an example of natural law), though anything can mess with it via the common sense rule; if the Resonance is calm, quiet stillness then Forces can mess that up the same way a rave can.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah. <br /> <br /> Looks like my planned-to-be homebrew Obrimos Legacy, the Children of Gaia, gets to do Resonance manipulation in addition to Rite-hacking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-03T09:49:02-07:00","id":1454138,"title":"","content":"You know, I've read this three times, and I still can't quite shake or grasp the feeling-nay, the <i>implications</i> of just how huge a drop these 30 pages are. I'm gonna need to read it a couple more times before I can safely discern whether it's a feeling or a fact, but something about this product feels like a game changer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-05-2021, 03:14 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-04T05:33:07-07:00","id":1454193,"title":"","content":"There is a lot packed in here and I do get the feeling that they were holding back stuff due to the 'release rule'; (until the new edition is in print, you can't reference too much of the new things).<br /> I did think it would be larger, but dang they fit a lot in there.<br /> <br /> Not sure about the omission of Sorcery Rites but since everything else is pretty much covered (references to earlier cross-over material aside), I am more than happy with it. We got rules for shared groups (yoinking that for Beast), the explict death of Supernal cosmological supremacy while making them great for mixed groups (including what Uratha rites and Sin-Eater necromancy look like), new merits that include telepathic communication, joining other species social splats and hunter's 'teaching' Tactics to non-hunters.<br /> <br /> Oh, almost forgot...there is so much on souls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-04T09:10:48-07:00","id":1454208,"title":"","content":"One of the questions I am sitting with is in regards to ephemeral entities connected to some of the gamelines that Mages can manipulate..specifically hedge ghosts, qashmallim, and angels. Could one with Life 5 and Fate 5 create an Elpidos for example...hell let's take it up a notch using the same Arcanums to take Pyros out of an Elpidos and then try to use the two Arcanums in conjunction to use that &quot;loose&quot; pyros to birth one? If one could harm or heal one with the spheres I just wondered if that goes all the way up to creating one. <br /> <br /> So I wonder what the conclusion will be there <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8100-caedus","name":"Caedus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"300"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-04T11:18:42-07:00","id":1454222,"title":"","content":"I really like the Player's Guide to the Contagion, but I'm a bit sad that it doesn't provide more information for Mage + Mummy crossovers. I'd really liked an official answer about the nature of Sekhem, Dedwen and Heka, and ways for Mages to manipulate those.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-04T11:22:59-07:00","id":1454223,"title":"","content":"It doesn't provide that information directly; but that's because that information has already been published. Still, I kind of wish they had provided a capsule summary of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-04T13:12:19-07:00","id":1454230,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1454223#post1454223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't provide that information directly; but that's because that information has already been published. Still, I kind of wish they had provided a capsule summary of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you show me where exactly? Princes of the Conquered Land only gives rules for manipulating Pillars, and not Sekhem, Heka or Dedwen.<br /> <br /> Of course you could say that Pillars are a kind of refined Sekhem, but it is also possible to come across pure undiluted Sekhem, for example by shattering a Relic. What is this Sekhem in Mage terms (a form of resonance? something stranger?), how would a Mage contain it, and what could he use it for?<br /> <br /> Heka could for most intents and purposes be treated as Resonance I guess, and Dedwen is quite abstract, so it could not be detectable by Mages at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-04T14:21:47-07:00","id":1454240,"title":"","content":"As far as I can tell, the only game systems associated with Sekhem, Heka, or Dedwen is that Sekhem is Mummy's power stat; and I'm loathe to have anything less than an Imperial Arcanum mess with a power stat. Heka and Dedwen inform us about how the Arisen see the world; but they don't have any game systems (that I know of) associated with them, so I don't know how you'd go about bringing Mage's game systems to bear on them directly. I could see, for instance, a mage using Prime to manipulate that thing that mummies call \u201cdedwen\u201d; though in Mage terms, it would be a matter of manipulating the abstract concept of \u201cvalue\u201d or \u201cutility\u201d \u2014 which is very much <i>not</i> the typical view of Prime and might need an Attainment to do. Or I could see a mage using Space to manipulate the mystical connections that the Arisen call \u201cheka\u201d.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-04T14:40:17-07:00","id":1454243,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caedus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1454208#post1454208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One of the questions I am sitting with is in regards to ephemeral entities connected to some of the gamelines that Mages can manipulate..specifically hedge ghosts, qashmallim, and angels. Could one with Life 5 and Fate 5 create an Elpidos for example...hell let's take it up a notch using the same Arcanums to take Pyros out of an Elpidos and then try to use the two Arcanums in conjunction to use that &amp;quot;loose&amp;quot; pyros to birth one? If one could harm or heal one with the spheres I just wondered if that goes all the way up to creating one. <br /> <br /> So I wonder what the conclusion will be there <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Mages could already create wolf-themed shapeshifters via Life magic and figure out ways to cram spirit powers there via Spirit magic, but the resulting creature wouldn\u2019t be Uratha. I suspect something similar would happen here too. Especially with qashmallim and angels. <br /> <br /> Not that it\u2019d bother mages, nor stop them <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-04T14:57:04-07:00","id":1454245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1454240#post1454240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As far as I can tell, the only game systems associated with Sekhem, Heka, or Dedwen is that Sekhem is Mummy's power stat; and I'm loathe to have anything less than an Imperial Arcanum mess with a power stat. Heka and Dedwen inform us about how the Arisen see the world; but they don't have any game systems (that I know of) associated with them, so I don't know how you'd go about bringing Mage's game systems to bear on them directly. I could see, for instance, a mage using Prime to manipulate that thing that mummies call \u201cdedwen\u201d; though in Mage terms, it would be a matter of manipulating the abstract concept of \u201cvalue\u201d or \u201cutility\u201d \u2014 which is very much <i>not</i> the typical view of Prime and might need an Attainment to do. Or I could see a mage using Space to manipulate the mystical connections that the Arisen call \u201cheka\u201d.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are correct in that Mummy does not have many game systems related to Heka, Dedwen and free Sekhem (as in, not the power stat of a Mummy), and that much of their treatment is more philosophical. According to alchemists, it is possible to transmute Dedwen into Sekhem, but that is more of a view as to how Sekhem comes to be. Heka is related to the flow of Sekhem in the world, specifically Geomancy, Ley Lines (Sekhem flows) and the flow of life energy within the body (which sounds like the meridians from Qigong). This also wouldn't necessarily need rules, as long as you would have rules for Sekhem itself.<br /> <br /> In addition to Sekhem as a power stat, Mummy treats Sekhem as a property of objects and the world around us, that flows and can be focussed in objects or corpses to create Vessels or Amkhata. The main description from the text is <i>&quot;Sekhem is the mystical energy emanating from all living things, allowing for the free flow of feelings and recollection in the universe. Revealing itself through passionate moments and intense memories, it subtly alters the environment as it coalesces. It brightens the light during a joyful birth. It thickens the air after a painful argument.&quot;</i> Also, according to the text about vessels it causes curses when concentrated.<br /> <br /> This sounds like something Mages should be able to interact with, possibly with some combination of Prime, Time and Fate, as Sekhem carries Resonance, history and curses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-04T15:12:56-07:00","id":1454249,"title":"","content":"Space should be in there, too: if you read up on it, it's not entirely about geometry (though there's a lot of that in there, and should be quite relevant to the Guild that is the primary cultivator of heka); it's also about the web of values (my term for it): a sympathetic connection exists between a person and a thing when that thing is important to that person, making it a kind of measure of what the person values \u2014 a very \u201cdedwen\u201d-like concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-04T15:22:27-07:00","id":1454250,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Penta</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1454245#post1454245\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This sounds like something Mages should be able to interact with, possibly with some combination of Prime, Time and Fate, as Sekhem carries Resonance, history and curses.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Eras Companion, Princes of the Conquered Lands, &quot;Crossover in the Conquered Land: Mana and Pillars&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Arisen believe Sekhem, and the Pillars of its divided power, are the stuff of Creation.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Eras, To The Strongest, Sidebar: &quot;Those Who Cross Over&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In contemporary terms, Sekhem is not \u201cSupernal,\u201d but the stuff of existence as it actually manifests. Awakened magic interacts with it like a smith holding tongs, while the Predynastic ancients [of Irem] preferred to grab this molten stuff with the spiritual equivalent of their bare hands.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages attempting to leverage Pillar points have to store them in places and objects whose Resonance matches the theme of the Pillar and create artificial Vestiges in doing so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-04T15:35:11-07:00","id":1454252,"title":"","content":"Good points. It would be nice if this, or a summary of it, was consolidated in one place\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-05T03:05:27-07:00","id":1454271,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1454250#post1454250\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages attempting to leverage Pillar points have to store them in places and objects whose Resonance matches the theme of the Pillar and create artificial Vestiges in doing so.</div> </div> </div> </div>So maybe a Mage attempting to leverage Sekhem dots (for example after canibalizing relics), would also have to store them, creating an artificial Relic? Sounds quite dangerous and/or impossible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-05T09:10:04-07:00","id":1454281,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1454252#post1454252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good points. It would be nice if this, or a summary of it, was consolidated in one place\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Particularly in light of the fact that the first section of the book, the general FAQ, came right out and said that it was reprinting information from existing books for ease of reference. To then not do so in the rest of the book is an\u2026interesting\u2026design choice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/743-exploding-frogs","name":"Exploding Frogs","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar743_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"54"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-05T15:19:02-07:00","id":1454307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Exploding Frogs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1454281#post1454281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Particularly in light of the fact that the first section of the book, the general FAQ, came right out and said that it was reprinting information from existing books for ease of reference. To then not do so in the rest of the book is an\u2026interesting\u2026design choice.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure if they will do anything about that at this stage, but it seems worth pointing that out in an errata form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-06T13:10:18-07:00","id":1454376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1454193#post1454193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the explict death of Supernal cosmological supremacy.</div> </div> </div> </div>What did they mean by this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23821-rathford","name":"Rathford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23821_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-06T14:43:33-07:00","id":1454380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1454193#post1454193\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the explict death of Supernal cosmological supremacy while making them great for mixed groups (including what Uratha rites and Sin-Eater necromancy look like)</div> </div> </div> </div>Joining the question of poster above - what does it mean? I am very interested in crossover material, running various crossovers with Mage all the time, but I am really not interested in material subverting or scrapping Mage cosmology. This could be a deal breaker for me to pass on the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-06T15:17:48-07:00","id":1454382,"title":"","content":"Clarifying a little bit more:<br /> <br /> The Supernal Cosmological Supremacy is a (incorrect) perspective that used to plague the forums that basically posited that everything was under the purview of the Awakened and that all things could be correlated to their cosmological mapping of the universe. It was a big enough problem that it affected the writing of Promethean and Chnageling and was a big pain in the ass for anyone who was there.<br /> <br /> It doesn't really happen now, since Second Edition made it very clear that it's entire point was that the universe is filled with non-supernal things and mages hunt them down for occult power, and the Contagion PG by thoroughly drawing the limits of the supernal regarding other gamelines.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Clarifying a little more: Supernal Cosmological Supremacy led to some dumb ideas that Vampire was the Stygia game and Werewolf was the Primal Wild game, so Promethean must be the Aether game, because it had angels, the &quot;IS CHANGELING ARCADIA MAGE ARCADIA&quot; kept long legs because of this stance, and people were bending themselves in knots trying to figure out how Hunter was the Pandemonium game, with a lot of really stupid ideas for how it would be.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile, there was also this &quot;Goku can beat everybody up&quot; sort of frain in the threads about how mages basically had all power over every other monster's power and could just stop them doing their thing by using Death or Fatge or Spirit, whatever.<br /> <br /> If you're looking at this while squinting and going huh, that's because this was perpetuated by people who didn't really understand Mage, it's world, or how magic works, which is half their fault and half Mage First Edition didn't always explain itself in the best way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 12-19-2021, 02:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-06T15:26:38-07:00","id":1454384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1454382#post1454382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Clarifying a little bit more:<br /> <br /> The Supernal Cosmological Supremacy is a (incorrect) perspective that used to plague the forums basically posited that everything was under the purview of the Awakened and that all things could be correlated to their cosmological mapping of the universe. It was a big enough problem that it affected the writing of Promethean and Chnageling and was a big pain in the ass for anyone who was there.<br /> <br /> It doesn't really happen now, since Second Edition made it very clear that it's entire point was that the universe is filled with non-supernal things and mages hunter them down for occult power, and the Contagion PG by thoroughly drawing the limits of the supernal regarding other gamelines.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aha, got it, thanks. Yeah, that doesn't bother me a lot, and it was explicitly stated in Second Edition what not all weirdness has a source in Supernal. Does it mean that some Fallen (crossover) things are cosmological blanks for the Awakened; that there is no Supernal Symbols describing them as part of Tapesty? Or it just means that Supernal Symbols can't describe them fully in context of Supernal? Or neither?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-06T15:33:36-07:00","id":1454385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1454384#post1454384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aha, got it, thanks. Yeah, that doesn't bother me a lot, and it was explicitly stated in Second Edition what not all weirdness has a source in Supernal. Does it mean that some Fallen (crossover) things are cosmological blanks for the Awakened; that there is no Supernal Symbols describing them as part of Tapesty? Or it just means that Supernal Symbols can't describe them fully in context of Supernal? Or neither?</div> </div> </div> </div>It means the Fallen World has a <i>lot more</i> elements at play in it than Supernal Light and Fallen Shadows. THe world is as much occult matrices and Sekhem and the Wyrd and Vitae as it is the Supernal, Abyssal, and Astral, and these things aren't connected (unless, of course, they somehow are, but that's a table matter).<br /> <br /> THe Supernal is articulation and vocabulary. The Fallen World has things it doesn't yet have words for. EDIT: and heading off possible questions, the Abyss is a thing/are things/actually aren't things or a thing where any word you apply to it is just very clearly always gonna be the wrong word because it's not actually a thing but is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-06-2021, 07:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-06T16:10:44-07:00","id":1454388,"title":"","content":"It's mostly an artifact of Mage 1st being compared at first to Ascension, which had a wide-ranging take on the fundamental nature of reality. Whereas Mage 1st+ or Mage 2nd really emphasize the uncertainty and how the cosmology is crazy-go-nuts. The supernal is a map, not the territory.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":543,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","user":"Professor Phobos","date":". 07-06-2021, 07:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-06T16:24:33-07:00","id":1454390,"title":"","content":"I'm interested in how, apparently, slashers have no souls. They are, in a sense, more inhuman than Beasts, who have a<i> replacement </i>for their souls.<br /> <br /> That is...intriguing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.us/a/img824/1346/mosz.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/180-leliel","name":"Leliel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar180_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-06T16:33:05-07:00","id":1454392,"title":"","content":"In a nutshell: there's a view out there that the Supernal is the underlying reality and that everything derives from it. This view even has its in-game proponents: the Seers of the Throne, an Order in the setting that worships Ascended Beings known as the Exarchs and who claim that everything in the Fallen World rightfully belongs to them. <br /> <br /> There's also the Free Council, which believes that the Supernal exists <i>because of</i> the so-called Fallen World, pointing to the fact that Supernal symbols can change in response to human innovations. To them, the proper order of this is that humans should be viewed as the center of things, and Supernal symbols should be viewed as tools that they wield. <br /> <br /> That said, the view of the bulk of Mage's Orders is that the Supernal symbols and the Phenomenal World exist in a symbiosis, with a sort of chicken-and-egg relationship: altering either affects the other, and trying to set up one as superior to the other is a mistake. Supernal symbols provide the handles that mages use to manipulate the Fallen World, so if course mages tend to put a lot of importance on them. But the Supernal is of central importance <i>to mages</i>; is not of central importance <i>overall</i>. <br /> <br /> That is, Supernatural Phenomena aren't a subset of Supernal Magic; Supernal Magick parallels supernatural phenomena. Because of this parallel nature, there <i>will</i> be Supernal symbols correlating with everything found in the Fallen World; but some are going to be harder to get a handle on than others. Mummy's metaphysics, in particular, seems to be particularly resistant to Supernal manipulations: despite much of their metaphysics being rooted in issues of time, Time magic is remarkably ineffective against it. <br /> <br /> It also puts assertions such as the one from the Dark Ages line that the Awakened manipulate Sekhem indirectly while the Arisen deals with it directly in a different light. I mean, it's <i>true</i>; but that's true of <i>everything</i> mages do: the whole basis of their metaphysics is to manipulate phenomena indirectly by manipulating the associated Supernal symbols. Sekhem isn't special in that regard.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-12-2021, 09:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-06T16:33:06-07:00","id":1454393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1454390#post1454390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm interested in how, apparently, slashers have no souls. They are, in a sense, more inhuman than Beasts, who have a<i> replacement </i>for their souls.<br /> <br /> That is...intriguing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Beasts are satiated by shock. Slashers are only satiated by murder.<br /> <br /> Never really hard to call the worse one between the two, to be honest, as that angle matters for the humanity/monstrosity argument.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-06-2021, 07:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-06T16:57:28-07:00","id":1454394,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leliel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1454390#post1454390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm interested in how, apparently, slashers have no souls. They are, in a sense, more inhuman than Beasts, who have a<i> replacement </i>for their souls.<br /> <br /> That is...intriguing.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I find interesting isn't the Beast vs. Slasher comparison; it's the Deviant vs. Slasher comparison, and the Soulless Condition vs. Slashers. Slashers have no souls; but they're not Soulless in the sense that the namesake Condition describes. But they're not people with <i>broken</i> souls, either; that would be the Deviants. If anything, they're more akin to the Tremere Liches from Mage, who have replaced their souls with a Hollow. I would say that, metaphysically, a Slasher's Undertaking serves a similar function to a Tremere's Hollow, in that it compensates for the lack of an actual soul to an extent but requires the indulgence of a fundamentally destructive activity (the theft and consumption of souls for the Tremere; murder for the Slasher). <br /> <br /> That said, I was a little surprised that the book made it that black and white. My inclination would have been to say that the first tier of Slashers (Rippers, if I recall correctly) still have (severely warped) souls; and that if there are Slashers who <i>don't</i> have souls, they'd be among the second-stage Slashers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-06T17:03:42-07:00","id":1454396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1454394#post1454394\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I find interesting isn't the Beast vs. Slasher comparison; it's the Deviant vs. Slasher comparison, and the Soulless Condition vs. Slashers. Slashers have no souls; but they're not Soulless in the sense that the namesake Condition describes. But they're not people with <i>broken</i> souls, either; that would be the Deviants. If anything, they're more akin to the Tremere Liches from Mage, who have replaced their souls with a Hollow. I would say that, metaphysically, a Slasher's Undertaking serves a similar function to a Tremere's Hollow, in that it compensates for the lack of an actual soul to an extent but requires the indulgence of a fundamentally destructive activity (the theft and consumption of souls for the Tremere; murder for the Slasher).<br /> <br /> That said, I was a little surprised that the book made it that black and white. My inclination would have been to say that the first tier of Slashers (Rippers, if I recall correctly) still have (severely warped) souls; and that if there are Slashers who <i>don't</i> have souls, they'd be among the second-stage Slashers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Space constraints being what they are, I think they trusted that people who knew more about it would likely houserule it so. Some blanket statements wear their obvious caveats on their sleeves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-06T18:35:35-07:00","id":1454405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1454392#post1454392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It also puts assertions such as the one from the Dark Ages line that the Awakened manipulate Sekhem indirectly whole the Arisen deals with it directly in a different light.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Shan'iatu. The bit in Dark Eras is talking about the Shan'iatu.<br /> <br /> Sekhem is raw existence-stuff that differentiates into the Pillars and dissipates back into its unrefined state when it's released from form through destruction. The Arcana no more allow a mage to manipulate it than they allow a Traveler to create a soul wholesale \u2014 they can mess with Pillars because Pillars are concrete enough phenomena to be described, hence &quot;Pillars <i>are</i> the world,&quot; but manipulating Sekhem directly would require something like the Tremere's focal project to manage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-06T20:22:17-07:00","id":1454412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dark Archon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1454384#post1454384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Aha, got it, thanks. Yeah, that doesn't bother me a lot, and it was explicitly stated in Second Edition what not all weirdness has a source in Supernal. Does it mean that some Fallen (crossover) things are cosmological blanks for the Awakened; that there is no Supernal Symbols describing them as part of Tapesty? Or it just means that Supernal Symbols can't describe them fully in context of Supernal? Or neither?</div> </div> </div> </div>It means that the relationship between a given thing and the Supernal doesn\u2019t necessarily go any deeper than \u201cThere\u2019s a symbol for it somewhere I guess.\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-06T20:51:35-07:00","id":1454414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sith_Happens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1454412#post1454412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It means that the relationship between a given thing and the Supernal doesn\u2019t necessarily go any deeper than \u201cThere\u2019s a symbol for it somewhere I guess.\u201d</div> </div> </div> </div>As above, so below, right? So, whatever exists / is phenomenal, presumably has symbolical description in the Supernal somewhere. But Duat is a Lower Depth, as Mage calls it, meaning mummies are backed by powers that lack description. I can only assume. Although mummies still exist in the Phenomenal as is, no?<br /> <br /> Thinking on it further, it seems very fitting that the magic of mummies has such resistances to the magic of mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23821,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23821-rathford","user":"Rathford","date":". 07-06-2021, 11:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23821-rathford","name":"Rathford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23821_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-06T21:38:30-07:00","id":1454417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1454414#post1454414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As above, so below, right? So, whatever exists / is phenomenal, presumably has symbolical description in the Supernal somewhere. But Duat is a Lower Depth, as Mage calls it, meaning mummies are backed by powers that lack description. I can only assume. Although mummies still exist in the Phenomenal as is, no?<br /> <br /> Thinking on it further, it seems very fitting that the magic of mummies has such resistances to the magic of mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lower Depths don't lack description-that's the Abyss. Lower Depths lack a certain aspect of reality. In the case of Duat, it's Sekhem/Pillars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-07-2021, 08:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-06T23:23:34-07:00","id":1454426,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1454392#post1454392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, the view of the bulk of Mage's Orders is that the Supernal symbols and the Phenomenal World exist in a symbiosis, with a sort of chicken-and-egg relationship: altering either affects the other, and trying to set up one as superior to the other is a mistake. Supernal symbols provide the handles that mages use to manipulate the Fallen World, so if course mages tend to put a lot of importance on them. But the Supernal is of central importance <i>to mages</i>; is not of central importance <i>overall</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I mean, kudos for devs for telling this outloud. But this isn't exactly a new take, which I expected from quote in my previous messages. Imperial Mysteries already cemented the importance of Phenomenal World for even the greatest archmages and Ascended Beings - you can't meaningfully &quot;fix&quot; the universe in desired state with Imperial Rites without preparing it first. So things stay more or less the same, the only change is status quo is <i>clarified</i> and re-stated again. I can live with that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11880-dark-archon","name":"Dark Archon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11880_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"348"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-07T00:14:53-07:00","id":1454431,"title":"","content":"I might be a bit late to the party (as in, my only exposure to mage supremacy being people who complain about it) but wouldn't the repetition of the fact that everything in the Fallen being reflected in the Supernal be the foundation for the claim that the Supernal governs everything? If anything in this booklet kills mage supremacy, it's probably the fact that <i>mages themselves</i> still can't directly mess with stuff like templates, and that none of the splats are exclusively tied to any of the Arcana.<br /> <br /> <br /> I like how they clarified the current state of aura powers, explained souls, and described different fuel traits in terms of the Arcana. Some of the explanations and descriptions aren't my preferred takes, but the only thing that actually bugs me is vampires having &quot;human souls&quot; with no explanation of how that's even remotely possible considering how the soul leaves upon death and the Embrace takes place after death. Often this takes place at the same event, but it can also be multiple days between the two. I much preferred the spoilered Nameless &amp; Accursed version (which is more detailed than the published Nameless &amp; Accursed version) where Kindred (as well as Uratha) had something that served the same purpose and was close enough to human/Awakened souls, but still distinctly different.<br /> The retcon that mages can't sever a Horror from a Beast also bugs me a bit, but only because it's a retcon and I definitely recognise that this is preferable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-07T03:48:37-07:00","id":1454436,"title":"","content":"I feel I may have accidentally derailed the thread. Sorry.<br /> <br /> In regards to vampires, I took the statement about having human souls to mean that there is little to no intrinsic difference between their souls and human souls. At least from a casual observer, since that can easily altered as needed in a game.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-07T11:12:57-07:00","id":1454465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1454431#post1454431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some of the explanations and descriptions aren't my preferred takes, but the only thing that actually bugs me is vampires having &amp;quot;human souls&amp;quot; with no explanation of how that's even remotely possible considering how the soul leaves upon death and the Embrace takes place after death. Often this takes place at the same event, but it can also be multiple days between the two.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just because a vampire has <i>a</i> human soul doesn\u2019t mean it\u2019s the <i>same</i> soul they had in life, and the possibility that it was <b>created</b> by the Embrace is one that should keep more than one other splat up at night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-07T17:13:43-07:00","id":1454483,"title":"","content":"There\u2019s a popular observation/interpretation that a vampire\u2019s Beast is basically an embodied Strix (or vice-versa; Strix being disembodied Beasts). <br /> <br /> With the Strix, there was another one of those \u2018possible truths\u2019 thing, with regards to the unique status of humans in the spirit world; the possibility that the Strix are (corrupt?) spirits of humans. (I think it was one of Rose Bailey\u2019s writings?)<br /> <br /> And now vampires are revealed to have something like a human soul. Hmm\u2026","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-07T17:35:10-07:00","id":1454486,"title":"","content":"My understanding from the reading the vampiric soul was not so much they have a <i>human</i> soul so much as a <i>human equivalent</i> soul, regarded not the same as, say, an Awakened soul or other things regarded in the same &quot;class&quot;.<br /> <br /> Again, with brevity of space in mind, it pays to give the benefit of the doubt that the material in the Contagion PG isn't there to destroy <i>all</i> mysteries or nuance associated with the various gamelines, so much as to provide the semblance of place in the larger picture of the Chronicles world as matters for the purposes of crossover necessarily interacting with said larger picture.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-07-2021, 09:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-07T22:00:07-07:00","id":1454500,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1454486#post1454486\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding from the reading the vampiric soul was not so much they have a <i>human</i> soul so much as a <i>human equivalent</i> soul, regarded not the same as, say, an Awakened soul or other things regarded in the same &amp;quot;class&amp;quot;.<br /> <br /> Again, with brevity of space in mind, it pays to give the benefit of the doubt that the material in the Contagion PG isn't there to destroy <i>all</i> mysteries or nuance associated with the various gamelines, so much as to provide the semblance of place in the larger picture of the Chronicles world as matters for the purposes of crossover necessarily interacting with said larger picture.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that vampires doesn t have an Oneiros and an access to Temenos, their souls are probably similar to human ones, but not equals","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-08T00:07:43-07:00","id":1454504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1454417#post1454417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Lower Depths don't lack description-that's the Abyss. Lower Depths lack a certain aspect of reality. In the case of Duat, it's Sekhem/Pillars.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It lacks descriptive time. It is timeless. That metaphorical light of the Supernal does not reach it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23821-rathford","name":"Rathford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23821_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-08T00:19:39-07:00","id":1454505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1454483#post1454483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There\u2019s a popular observation/interpretation that a vampire\u2019s Beast is basically an embodied Strix (or vice-versa; Strix being disembodied Beasts).</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a popular take, but it's based on the fact that Strix, consumate liars as they are, has claimed that's the case to vampires. In the 2e core book, a vampire's beast is written with the assumption that it's merely a representation of all the dark and predatory urges a vampire gains upon the Embrace (hunger for blood, need for dominance, fear of Banes, etc), and not an actual entity. While horrible and monstrous, these urges are deeply animalistic, in contrast to the vice-ridden and sadistic nature of the Strix. Also note that Strix are incapable of Frenzy while Frenzy is the primary outlet for the beast.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Neos01</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1454500#post1454500\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Considering that vampires doesn t have an Oneiros and an access to Temenos, their souls are probably similar to human ones, but not equals</div> </div> </div> </div>The state of the oneiros isn't that clear. It was stated by a dev who at the time also stated outright that they didn't have souls (and then changed his mind on the matter twice before N&amp;A came out). But they certainly don't connect to the Temenos, as that's exclusively for humans, mages and Beasts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-08T06:21:11-07:00","id":1454518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rathford</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1454504#post1454504\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It lacks descriptive time. It is timeless. That metaphorical light of the Supernal does not reach it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, that's foundationally <i>not true</i>. The Lower Depths aren't predicated on their relationship to Supernal, so the &quot;light&quot; of the Supernal being present or not is not what defines their status as Lower Depths. What defines the Lower Depths is what they lack in relationship to the Fallen/Phenomenal World, and this is one of those ways that reiterates that thinking about Mage Cosmology above all over cosmologies is incorrect, because while those things can be &quot;devoid of LIfe&quot; or &quot;devoid of Time&quot;, it can just as easily be &quot;devoid of Sekhem&quot; or &quot;devoid of Virtue&quot;*.<br /> <br /> Trying to make Lower Depths all about their non-relationship to the Supernal Realms is one of those things that happens when you try and make the whole of the Chronicles world about Mage, and that was demonstrably <i>not a good time</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 07-08-2021, 09:41 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-08T19:49:11-07:00","id":1454566,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1454505#post1454505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a popular take, but it's based on the fact that Strix, consumate liars as they are, has claimed that's the case to vampires. In the 2e core book, a vampire's beast is written with the assumption that it's merely a representation of all the dark and predatory urges a vampire gains upon the Embrace (hunger for blood, need for dominance, fear of Banes, etc), and not an actual entity. While horrible and monstrous, these urges are deeply animalistic, in contrast to the vice-ridden and sadistic nature of the Strix. Also note that Strix are incapable of Frenzy while Frenzy is the primary outlet for the beast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aw shucks. Forgot about frenzies <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-08T22:26:22-07:00","id":1454571,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1454518#post1454518\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, that's foundationally <i>not true</i>. The Lower Depths aren't predicated on their relationship to Supernal, so the &quot;light&quot; of the Supernal being present or not is not what defines their status as Lower Depths. What defines the Lower Depths is what they lack in relationship to the Fallen/Phenomenal World, and this is one of those ways that reiterates that thinking about Mage Cosmology above all over cosmologies is incorrect, because while those things can be &quot;devoid of LIfe&quot; or &quot;devoid of Time&quot;, it can just as easily be &quot;devoid of Sekhem&quot; or &quot;devoid of Virtue&quot;*.<br /> <br /> Trying to make Lower Depths all about their non-relationship to the Supernal Realms is one of those things that happens when you try and make the whole of the Chronicles world about Mage, and that was demonstrably <i>not a good time</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ironically, the common descriptive shorthand for the Lower Depths <i>also</i> isn't terribly useful except in abstract vagary: Duat, the Inferno, and whatever Dark Places the Strix come from <i>could</i> be described by their lacks, technically Arcana-oriented or otherwise, but for the most part, like other pure-negative descriptions, that doesn't tell you anything worthwhile about them.<br /> <br /> The Lower Depths are off the map and want to eat you, in a way that does not feed back into a larger ecosystem unless something major is playing a bigger game with its cut of the take. Visits are usually one-way trips, barring those cases where astral projection and a special relationship are involved. They are thin realities that are hostile to human life in the way outer space or the depths of the ocean are \u2014 there is a pressure differential at work not unlike the one separating the Supernal and Phenomenal, and there's only so much you can do without magic to compensate for the fact that you need to breathe and Flatland #42564 has no concept of air.<br /> <br /> The ancient summation still holds: <i>Not all of them are evil, but none of them are good.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-10T13:19:04-07:00","id":1454656,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1454431#post1454431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">the only thing that actually bugs me is vampires having &quot;human souls&quot; with no explanation of how that's even remotely possible considering how the soul leaves upon death and the Embrace takes place after death.</div> </div> </div> </div>In the past I've had thoughts to the effect that Requiem seems to have a subtext that vampires aren't quite as inhuman as they try to convince themselves that they are, to the point that the way some of the super ancient ones seem to be weirdly normal and overcome some of the usual impositions comes across as ones who, with the benefit of time, manage to get over themselves.<br /> <br /> The notion that the composition of a vampire amounts to somebody who died but had freaky blood magic ensure that their soul stuck around when it wasn't supposed to, that they're kind of tangled up inside themselves, to me that would lend a certain context to the interplay between Kindred drives and human hang-ups.<br /> <br /> As far as unconventional Embraces go, I would picture the mystery of the soul's departure (and arrival, for that matter) as also affording leeway for its return. Possibly along lines of it existing in a layer of reality where such causal terms may not strictly apply.<br /> <br /> It would play off of my perspective on Vampire where they seem like the most straightforward on the surface but when you delve in things get all twisted and freakish, whether it's the diverse possibilities of Devotions and Bloodlines, the qualities that can be harnessed as Sorcery, the enforcement power that can arise from their Covenants, basically everything in Coils of the Dragon from the ground up, or all of the bizarre cults and monstrosities that branch away across their history. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-22T18:12:46-07:00","id":1455404,"title":"","content":"This renewed discussion makes me regret a little only backing at the manuscript preview tier. Ah well, it's not as though I could have simply chosen to have more money then. Is there any word on Deviants and Kinship?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-23T05:07:29-07:00","id":1455433,"title":"","content":"I think I heard we have stuff about Resonance here, but does the crossover rules section have word on Sympathy too? (Mostly from a Mage perspective, but about interaction with other games, like Vampire and blood sympathy)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-23T09:53:53-07:00","id":1455444,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1455433#post1455433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I heard we have stuff about Resonance here, but does the crossover rules section have word on Sympathy too? (Mostly from a Mage perspective, but about interaction with other games, like Vampire and blood sympathy)</div> </div> </div> </div>It is a substantial subset of the crossover rules for Mage. Beasts, deviants, vampires, changelings, demons, and Bound all have particulars of how they interact with sympathy addressed in their respective subsections.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-23T14:03:36-07:00","id":1455465,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1455404#post1455404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This renewed discussion makes me regret a little only backing at the manuscript preview tier. Ah well, it's not as though I could have simply chosen to have more money then. Is there any word on Deviants and Kinship?</div> </div> </div> </div>What sort of word are you looking for?<br /> <br /> Because if it's &quot;Are Deviants kin?&quot;, the answer is yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-23T17:44:13-07:00","id":1455471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1455465#post1455465\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What sort of word are you looking for?<br /> <br /> Because if it's &quot;Are Deviants kin?&quot;, the answer is yes.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty much it. I figured that would be the case, but the Broken have a lot of unique stuff going on, and so didn't want to assume.<br /> <br /> Changelings and sympathy. . . Does that mean we get a preview of Dramaturgy?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-23T23:20:03-07:00","id":1455482,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1455471#post1455471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Changelings and sympathy. . . Does that mean we get a preview of Dramaturgy?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah. Active Contract Loopholes, however, show up to the Fate and Space spells for looking at sympathetic connections, and the ties a changeling has with their Icons are substantial.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-27T15:39:00-07:00","id":1455681,"title":"","content":"So while the &quot;how does Mage interact with everything&quot; discussion is nice, did the stuff on other supernaturals interacting with each other turn out as interesting? Like the stuff on joining different groups or the new shared Merits and rules?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12743-kamenhero25","name":"kamenhero25","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12743_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-27T19:24:14-07:00","id":1455693,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kamenhero25</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1455681#post1455681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So while the &quot;how does Mage interact with everything&quot; discussion is nice, did the stuff on other supernaturals interacting with each other turn out as interesting? Like the stuff on joining different groups or the new shared Merits and rules?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm still chewing on all of that. When I said it feels like a game changer, it's those last ten pages that my brain scrambling to untangle the consequences.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-27T20:37:56-07:00","id":1455699,"title":"","content":"My group has been having a lot of fun with all the cool story possibilities introduced by explicitly saying vampires can ghoul <i>everybody</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Posting gives me anxiety, but I'm still happy to be here</i><br /> Habitual Lurker, Vengrel Liker, Acolyte Apologist, She/Her","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25955-somethingfishy","name":"SomethingFishy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25955_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-27T23:01:46-07:00","id":1455702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SomethingFishy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1455699#post1455699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My group has been having a lot of fun with all the cool story possibilities introduced by explicitly saying vampires can ghoul <i>everybody</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>They can do <i>what</i>?!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12743-kamenhero25","name":"kamenhero25","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12743_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-28T16:26:46-07:00","id":1455734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kamenhero25</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1455681#post1455681\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So while the &quot;how does Mage interact with everything&quot; discussion is nice, did the stuff on other supernaturals interacting with each other turn out as interesting? Like the stuff on joining different groups or the new shared Merits and rules?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it has those. I thought that was mentioned upthread, but it can be easy to miss in the tide of posts.<br /> I do wish we got more on multisplat groups, but we have enough. It can vary by splat though; no Mage or Begotten can join a Changleing Court via Mantle but Court Goodwill is fine, thus represents how non-Changelings join.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-28T17:42:02-07:00","id":1455738,"title":"","content":"My only gripe so far about the multi-splat groups is that they spend a whole section discussing what they should be called. To me, that is the least important thing to discuss. I would much rather have had a bit less focus on the naming of what other game systems call a party, and instead a little more focused on the special benefits that the existing kind of parties can accomplish (such as a branded throng, or a symbolic cabal) and what if anything a non-standard member of the throng / cabal/whatever could do to become part of the mystically empowered team. <br /> <br /> The subsequent sections that go into what to do about the various benefits different kinds of groups provide and how to blend them is considerably more interesting. And it has a fairly extensive section on shared merits, with a particular focus on how to combine different kinds of safe spaces. The sections about how outsiders can become involved in various traditionally single type organizations is interesting, such as non-demons joining agendas, none werewolves joining lodges, and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-07-29T11:00:25-07:00","id":1455759,"title":"","content":"Is there possibly a quick, couple of sentences, summary of the contagions in Chapter Five somewhere?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12488-jeremysbrain","name":"Jeremysbrain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T11:45:40-07:00","id":1456443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kamenhero25</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1455702#post1455702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They can do <i>what</i>?!</div> </div> </div> </div>See... I'm surprised this is the ONLY mention of this change in this thread thus far. I am a bit late to checking out the PDF evidently, but while I agree with ArcaneArts that the last ten pages are a game-changer, I honestly think that's nothing compared to this change - and the fact that it's only a small part of the change that was made. I am not sure how much we're supposed to discuss in public though, but this, right here, is the thing that has WAY bigger implications, IMO.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T12:56:47-07:00","id":1456450,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EndlessKng</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1456443#post1456443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> See... I'm surprised this is the ONLY mention of this change in this thread thus far. I am a bit late to checking out the PDF evidently, but while I agree with ArcaneArts that the last ten pages are a game-changer, I honestly think that's nothing compared to this change - and the fact that it's only a small part of the change that was made. I am not sure how much we're supposed to discuss in public though, but this, right here, is the thing that has WAY bigger implications, IMO.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, for me it's both unchaining vampires and letting them flex in ways that are appropriate for them....and at the same time reintroducing the &quot;Every mage is a ghoul&quot; problem I ran into all the time with World players and fear running into for anyone familiar with this supplement.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, the proportion in comparison, so I can carefully introduce that factor as I care to.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T15:11:02-07:00","id":1456457,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1456450#post1456450\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, for me it's both unchaining vampires and letting them flex in ways that are appropriate for them....and at the same time reintroducing the &quot;Every mage is a ghoul&quot; problem I ran into all the time with World players and fear running into for anyone familiar with this supplement.<br /> <br /> Fortunately, the proportion in comparison, so I can carefully introduce that factor as I care to.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I suppose I'm more concerned about the BROADER implications of that question in the FAQ. Mage Ghouls are a possibility, but that's nothing compared to the fact that ALL such crossovers are, at least as far as the official word is concerned, open all the way. <br /> <br /> Then again, it's a table rule thing, and I doubt there will be further official support. But still, big change to codify. They had been slowly killing it as they said, but honestly the rules still implied that there were some barriers and those are just... not a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1407-endlesskng","name":"EndlessKng","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"335"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T16:12:52-07:00","id":1456467,"title":"","content":"Ah; so <i>that's</i> the concern? Multi-splat characters? In a supplement about crossovers? If you're going to knock the walls down, this would be the place. <br /> <br /> Frankly, my own concerns about it are twofold: first, the game system complications of someone having, say, both Sekhem <i>and</i> a dot of Blood Potency; do too much blending, and the character sheet becomes a nightmare to manage. Second, can the potentially clashing themes be synergized into something interesting? <br /> <br /> Still, if you <i>can</i> synergize the concepts, and you don't find the mesh of traits overwhelming, and the group is okay with it, why not?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-09T17:36:20-07:00","id":1456478,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1456467#post1456467\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah; so <i>that's</i> the concern? Multi-splat characters? In a supplement about crossovers? If you're going to knock the walls down, this would be the place.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel like this dismisses the <i>actual</i> gist of the last third section's full weight. Multi-splat characters are interesting, even a wrinkle I've played with, but no.<br /> <br /> What the Contagion PG feels like is a breaking down of the last barrier to what Chronicles wants to say. World start off in a highly regimented world view that broke down as time went on, a point of view that Chronicles started with-that everyone belongs in the same universe, but has their own reasons for keeping to themselves.<br /> <br /> The Contagion PG finally says &quot;Fuuuuuuuck that&quot;, because now there are changelings in Mage Orders, werewolves intgrating Lodges with Changeling Orders, Beasts in covenants and vampires in in broods, demons have outsiders in their Agencies, Guilds have demons in their rank-<br /> <br /> THe <i>last</i> barrier towards Chronicles' Archetypalism versus World's Specificity has been <i>breached</i>. Chronicles is now a full on global setting, where you really just can't expect any group of monsters to just be one type, where a game with nothing but one type of monster is no longer what's expected, even desired.<br /> <br /> And it's a minor breach, in comparison to a lot of the rest of the book, and much more on how this is a niche product for a high-level-of-Chronicles-literacy-but it's <i>enough</i>.<br /> <br /> It's not going to turn out this way, but it feels like the insularity of gameline as gameline is now strikingly fluid, and Chronicles sort just has what it need to be fucking weird and experimental and trying and consequential in a way it......has been before, but not on this subject.<br /> <br /> The world doesn't need it's members to be a character <i>made</i> to fit the conflict that <i>asks for characters made for it</i>.<br /> <br /> The world, post Contagion, and VERY DEFINITELY Post-ContagionPG, has stopped being about persons in particulars, and more about struggle and responses, annnnnnd....<br /> <br /> I both love and hate that approach. I lean more into it than I hate it, but, like-<br /> <br /> I can't live in a world with it's walls anymore, even on Beast where that was it's own fluid shit.<br /> <br /> And that is exciting, and scary, and above all else, <i>really interesting.</i> It suggests a 3rd edition that does away with the semi-wiped away Y-splat, a game that is as much about monsters just grouping under trees while the rain is blood while ancient monster conspiracies of fae word and vampire blood and Uratha carnality and Awakened lusts and Unchained schemes and Arisen Schemes and Beast familiarity and Promethean hunger and hunter resistance and Sin-Eater acceptance and Deviant drive all coalesce into weird and impossible shapes.<br /> <br /> The world no longer feels <i>isolated</i>, and as someone who was <i>always</i> slipping in reminders that no splat was alone in any game, that's <i>fucking huge</i>.<br /> <br /> On record, I dunno if that's a good thing or not. I like it, but I can see the trades.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 08-09-2021, 09:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-11T20:54:17-07:00","id":1456634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kamenhero25</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1455702#post1455702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They can do <i>what</i>?!</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically there's nothing now stopping your Changeling character from being a Sleepwalker (or even Proximi), Wolf-Blooded, Ghoul, and Stigmatic other than the Clarity damage it will do to your Storyteller","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2384-aurumae","name":"Aurumae","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2384_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-11T22:03:13-07:00","id":1456637,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aurumae</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1456634#post1456634\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Technically there's nothing now stopping your Changeling character from being a Sleepwalker -</div> </div> </div> </div>Mild correction-there is something <i>now</i> stopping your Changeling from being a Sleepwalker, and that's that all supernatural's were Sleepwalkers <i>loooong</i> before this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-12T05:19:34-07:00","id":1456645,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1456637#post1456637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mild correction-there is something <i>now</i> stopping your Changeling from being a Sleepwalker, and that's that all supernatural's were Sleepwalkers <i>loooong</i> before this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, what? Am I reading something wrong, or is there now some way for a changeling to be <i>not</i> a Sleepwalker? As in, a changeling being a Sleeper?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-12T06:25:18-07:00","id":1456653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>21C Hermit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1456645#post1456645\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wait, what? Am I reading something wrong, or is there now some way for a changeling to be <i>not</i> a Sleepwalker? As in, a changeling being a Sleeper?</div> </div> </div> </div>THere is <i>not</i> a way for a changeling to be a Sleeper.<br /> <br /> The point is that supernatural entities, including all of the major gameline protagonists barring Hunter, have counted as Sleepwalkers since *checks notes* Mage the Awakening Corebook, First Edition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-12T06:35:19-07:00","id":1456655,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1456653#post1456653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">THere is <i>not</i> a way for a changeling to be a Sleeper.<br /> <br /> The point is that supernatural entities, including all of the major gameline protagonists barring Hunter, have counted as Sleepwalkers since *checks notes* Mage the Awakening Corebook, First Edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, so it\u2019s just as I already knew. My bad. My logic engine must\u2019ve fried out. Gotta go to the nearest Logistics Infrastructure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-12T06:47:49-07:00","id":1456659,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1456653#post1456653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">THere is <i>not</i> a way for a changeling to be a Sleeper.<br /> <br /> The point is that supernatural entities, including all of the major gameline protagonists barring Hunter, have counted as Sleepwalkers since *checks notes* Mage the Awakening Corebook, First Edition.</div> </div> </div> </div>And the contagion Chronicles players guide recommends getting rid of the hunter exception, at least within the players group, as quickly as possible. Hopefully, my suggested errata about pointing out a sleepwalker merit (fitful slumber) from M2e that's particularly appropriate for this purpose will get accepted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","user":"Dataweaver","date":". 08-12-2021, 10:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-08-12T08:07:10-07:00","id":1456663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1299967-contagion-chronicle-kickstarter?p=1456659#post1456659\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And the contagion Chronicles players guide recommends getting rid of the hunter exception, at least within the players group, as quickly as possible. Hopefully, my suggested errata about pointing out a sleepwalker merit (fitful slumber) from M2e that's particularly appropriate for this purpose will get accepted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heading off the old arguments that might be buried here, it should be pointed out that Hunters being sleepwalkers has more to do with facilitating the crossover, and more importantly Hunters being Sleepwalkers does not remove the Catch-22 of Hunters basically being up a creek when hunting the Awakened. <i>Nothing</i> about the Hunter/Mage Argument has changed with the Contagion PG.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"react